  'Option B (Oversampling) is the correct technique to address class imbalance by increasing the number of samples in the minority class, either by duplicating existing samples or generating synthetic ones (e.g., SMOTE). Option A (Undersampling) reduces the number of samples in the majority class. Option C (Feature selection) and Option D (Dimensionality reduction) are techniques for managing the number of features, not for handling class imbalance.',
