  'Option C (correct) is the F1-Score, which is particularly suitable for binary classification problems with imbalanced datasets because it provides a harmonic mean of precision and recall, giving a more balanced view of performance than accuracy alone. Option A (Accuracy) can be misleading with imbalanced datasets. Option B (MAE) and Option D (RMSE) are metrics for regression problems, not classification.',
