  '{2}'::int[],
  'Option C (correct) describes overfitting, a common issue where a model learns the training data too well, including its noise, leading to poor generalization on new, unseen data. Option A (Underfitting) and Option B (High bias) describe a model that is too simple and fails to capture the underlying patterns. Option D (Data leakage) is a data preparation issue, not directly a model performance issue in this context.',
