  '{1}'::int[],
  'Option B (correct) accurately describes the primary use of a confusion matrix, which is a table used to evaluate the performance of a classification model. It provides a detailed breakdown of correct and incorrect predictions for each class. Option A is typically done with scatter plots or histograms. Option C is addressed by methods like the elbow method or silhouette score. Option D is usually visualized with loss curves.',
