  '{1}'::int[],
  'Option B (To detect bias in machine learning models and provide feature attribution for explainability) accurately describes the primary purpose of Amazon SageMaker Clarify. It helps data scientists understand model predictions and identify potential biases in data or models. Option A describes SageMaker Automatic Model Tuning (HPO). Option C describes SageMaker Model Monitor. Option D describes SageMaker Experiments.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain15_3',
  NOW(),
  34,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_15_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_15_m_15_3_91',
  'A data scientist observes that their model''s training loss is continuously decreasing, but the validation loss has started to increase significantly. Which issue is the model MOST likely experiencing?',
  'mcq',
  '["Underfitting","Bias-variance tradeoff","Overfitting","Data leakage"]'::json,
  '{2}'::int[],
  'Option C (Overfitting) is the most likely issue. Overfitting occurs when a model learns the training data too well, including noise and specific patterns, leading to poor generalization on unseen data (reflected by increasing validation loss while training loss continues to decrease). Option A (Underfitting) would typically show high training and validation loss. Option B (Bias-variance tradeoff) is a general concept in model building, not a specific symptom like this. Option D (Data leakage) is a problem where information from the test set is inadvertently used during training, which could lead to artificially high validation scores, not necessarily increasing validation loss.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain15_3',
  NOW(),
  35,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_15_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

