INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_2_56',
  'Which AWS service is primarily used to store Docker images for machine learning models that will be deployed on Amazon SageMaker?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon ECR","Amazon S3","AWS Lambda","Amazon DynamoDB"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (Amazon ECR) is the correct service. Amazon Elastic Container Registry (ECR) is a fully managed Docker container registry that makes it easy for developers to store, manage, and deploy Docker container images. SageMaker often pulls model images directly from ECR. Option B (Amazon S3) is object storage, not a container registry. Option C (AWS Lambda) is a serverless compute service. Option D (Amazon DynamoDB) is a NoSQL database service.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  1,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_16_2',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_2_57',
  'Which AWS service allows you to provision and manage your AWS infrastructure, including SageMaker resources, using declarative configuration files?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS CloudFormation","AWS Systems Manager","AWS Config","AWS OpsWorks"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (AWS CloudFormation) is the correct service for provisioning and managing AWS infrastructure as code using declarative templates. It allows you to define your resources, including Amazon SageMaker components, in a file and deploy them consistently. Option B (AWS Systems Manager) is for operational insights and management of resources. Option C (AWS Config) is for assessing, auditing, and evaluating the configurations of your AWS resources. Option D (AWS OpsWorks) is a configuration management service that uses Chef and Puppet.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  2,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_16_2',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_2_58',
  'Which AWS service is used to containerize machine learning models, ensuring consistent runtime environments across development and deployment stages?',
  'mcq',
  '["Docker with Amazon ECR","AWS Lambda","Amazon EC2","Amazon S3"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (Docker with Amazon ECR) is the correct approach. Docker is used to containerize applications, including ML models, packaging them with their dependencies into a consistent unit. Amazon ECR then stores these Docker images. Option B (AWS Lambda) is a serverless compute service, not for containerization itself. Option C (Amazon EC2) provides virtual servers, which can run containers, but EC2 itself doesn''t containerize. Option D (Amazon S3) is object storage.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  3,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_16_2',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_2_59',
  'What is the primary benefit of using AWS Cloud Development Kit (AWS CDK) for defining Amazon SageMaker infrastructure?',
  'mcq',
  '["It allows defining infrastructure using familiar programming languages.","It provides a visual drag-and-drop interface for resource creation.","It automatically optimizes model performance for deployment.","It manages data storage and retrieval for SageMaker notebooks."]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (It allows defining infrastructure using familiar programming languages) is the primary benefit of AWS CDK. It provides a high-level, object-oriented way to define cloud infrastructure, which then synthesizes into AWS CloudFormation templates. Option B describes visual tools, not CDK. Option C describes services like SageMaker Neo. Option D describes services like Amazon S3, which can be used with SageMaker notebooks.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  4,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_16_2',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_2_60',
  'Which AWS service is used to define auto-scaling policies for Amazon SageMaker endpoints to adjust capacity based on real-time traffic?',
  'mcq',
  '["Application Auto Scaling","AWS Auto Scaling","Amazon CloudWatch","AWS Systems Manager"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (Application Auto Scaling) is the service used to configure automatic scaling for various AWS resources, including Amazon SageMaker endpoints. It allows you to define scaling policies based on metrics like CPU utilization or invocation count. Option B (AWS Auto Scaling) is a broader term that encompasses Application Auto Scaling but is less specific for SageMaker endpoints. Option C (Amazon CloudWatch) is a monitoring service that provides metrics, but Application Auto Scaling acts on those metrics. Option D (AWS Systems Manager) is for operational management, not direct auto-scaling configuration.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  5,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_16_2',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_2_61',
  'What is a key advantage of defining machine learning infrastructure using Infrastructure as Code (IaC) tools like AWS CloudFormation?',
  'mcq',
  '["Ensures consistent and repeatable deployments.","Automatically optimizes model training performance.","Provides real-time monitoring of inference endpoints.","Manages data versioning for training datasets."]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (Ensures consistent and repeatable deployments) is a key advantage of Infrastructure as Code. By defining infrastructure in code, you can version control it, review changes, and deploy it consistently across different environments, eliminating manual errors. Option B relates to services like SageMaker training jobs or Neo. Option C relates to services like Amazon CloudWatch. Option D relates to data management strategies, not IaC itself.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  6,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_16_2',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_2_62',
  'What is the main purpose of containerizing a machine learning model using Docker?',
  'mcq',
  '["To ensure the model runs consistently across different environments.","To automatically scale the model''s inference endpoint.","To reduce the storage size of the model artifacts.","To encrypt the model''s parameters for security."]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (To ensure the model runs consistently across different environments) is the main purpose of containerization. Docker containers package the model, its dependencies, and configuration into a single, isolated unit, guaranteeing that it behaves the same regardless of where it''s deployed. Option B is handled by services like Application Auto Scaling. Option C is related to model optimization techniques like quantization, not containerization itself. Option D is handled by encryption services or methods.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  7,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_16_2',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_2_63',
  'When deploying a machine learning model on Amazon SageMaker, what is the purpose of configuring auto-scaling for the endpoint?',
  'mcq',
  '["To automatically adjust the number of instances based on inference traffic.","To automatically optimize the model for better performance.","To automatically encrypt the data transmitted to the endpoint.","To automatically version control the deployed model."]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (To automatically adjust the number of instances based on inference traffic) is the correct purpose of auto-scaling. It ensures that the endpoint has sufficient capacity to handle varying loads, preventing performance bottlenecks during peak times and reducing costs during low traffic periods. Option B relates to SageMaker Neo. Option C relates to security configurations. Option D relates to SageMaker Model Registry.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  8,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_16_2',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
