INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_2_65',
  'Which AWS service allows you to define your SageMaker infrastructure using Python or TypeScript, which then generates CloudFormation templates?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS Cloud Development Kit (AWS CDK)","AWS SDK for Python (Boto3)","AWS Command Line Interface (AWS CLI)","AWS Management Console"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (AWS Cloud Development Kit (AWS CDK)) is the correct tool. The AWS CDK allows developers to define cloud infrastructure using familiar programming languages like Python, TypeScript, Java, .NET, and Go, which then synthesizes into CloudFormation templates. Option B (AWS SDK for Python (Boto3)) is for interacting with AWS services programmatically, not defining infrastructure as code. Option C (AWS Command Line Interface (AWS CLI)) is for managing AWS services via command-line commands. Option D (AWS Management Console) is a web-based interface.',
