) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_2_68',
  'A data science team needs to manage multiple versions of their machine learning models, track their lineage, and implement an approval workflow before deployment to production. Which AWS service is specifically designed to meet these requirements for model governance?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon SageMaker Model Registry","Amazon ECR","AWS CodePipeline","Amazon EventBridge"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (Amazon SageMaker Model Registry) is the correct service. It provides a centralized repository to catalog models, manage their versions, track lineage, and implement approval workflows, which is essential for model governance and MLOps best practices. Option B (Amazon ECR) is a container registry for Docker images, not specifically for ML model versioning and governance. Option C (AWS CodePipeline) is a continuous delivery service used for automating release pipelines, but it doesn''t inherently provide model versioning or approval workflows. Option D (Amazon EventBridge) is a serverless event bus that connects application components, useful for triggering workflows but not for model governance itself.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  13,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_16_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_2_69',
  'A machine learning engineer needs to store Docker images for custom training and inference environments securely. These images will be used by Amazon SageMaker. Which AWS service should be used for this purpose?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS CodeBuild","Amazon ECR","Amazon S3","AWS Lambda"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (Amazon ECR) is the correct service. Amazon Elastic Container Registry (ECR) is a fully managed Docker container registry that makes it easy for developers to store, manage, and deploy Docker container images. It integrates seamlessly with Amazon SageMaker for custom environments. Option A (AWS CodeBuild) is a continuous integration service that compiles source code and runs tests, not for storing container images. Option C (Amazon S3) is object storage, which can store container image files but does not provide a managed Docker registry interface or features like image scanning and versioning. Option D (AWS Lambda) is a serverless compute service, not a storage service for Docker images.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  14,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_16_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_2_70',
  'A company wants to automate the provisioning of all AWS resources for their machine learning projects, including Amazon SageMaker endpoints and training jobs, to ensure consistency and repeatability. Which AWS service is best suited for defining and deploying this infrastructure as code?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS CodeBuild","Amazon EventBridge","AWS CloudFormation","Amazon ECR"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (AWS CloudFormation) is the correct service. AWS CloudFormation allows you to define your AWS infrastructure as code using templates, enabling automated and consistent provisioning of resources like Amazon SageMaker endpoints, training jobs, and other related services. Option A (AWS CodeBuild) is a continuous integration service for compiling code and running tests. Option B (Amazon EventBridge) is an event bus for connecting application components and triggering workflows, not for defining infrastructure. Option D (Amazon ECR) is a container registry for Docker images.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  15,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_16_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_2_71',
  'Which AWS service is specifically designed to orchestrate end-to-end machine learning workflows, including data processing, model training, and model evaluation, as a series of steps?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS CodePipeline","Amazon EventBridge","AWS Step Functions","Amazon SageMaker Pipelines"]'::json,
  '{3}',
  'Option D (Amazon SageMaker Pipelines) is the correct service. It is a purpose-built CI/CD service for machine learning that allows you to create, manage, and orchestrate end-to-end ML workflows as a series of steps, including data preparation, model training, and evaluation. Option A (AWS CodePipeline) is a general-purpose continuous delivery service. Option B (Amazon EventBridge) is an event bus for event-driven architectures. Option C (AWS Step Functions) is a serverless workflow service that can orchestrate distributed applications, but SageMaker Pipelines is specifically optimized for ML workflows.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  16,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_16_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_2_72',
  'A machine learning team wants to automate the process of building, testing, and deploying their models. They need a service that can integrate with their source code repository, run custom build commands, and then deploy the model to an Amazon SageMaker endpoint. Which AWS service combination is most appropriate for the build and test phase within an MLOps pipeline?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS CodeBuild integrated with Amazon SageMaker","Amazon EventBridge triggering AWS Lambda","Amazon S3 with AWS Glue","Amazon SageMaker Studio with manual deployments"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (AWS CodeBuild integrated with Amazon SageMaker) is the correct choice. AWS CodeBuild is a fully managed continuous integration service that compiles source code, runs tests, and produces deployable artifacts. It can be integrated into an MLOps pipeline (often orchestrated by AWS CodePipeline) to build model artifacts or Docker images and then deploy them to SageMaker. Option B (Amazon EventBridge triggering AWS Lambda) can be used for event-driven automation but is not primarily designed for the build and test phase of a CI/CD pipeline. Option C (Amazon S3 with AWS Glue) is typically used for data storage and ETL processes, not for building and testing model code. Option D (Amazon SageMaker Studio with manual deployments) involves manual steps, which goes against the goal of automation.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  17,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_16_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_2_73',
  'A machine learning team is struggling with inconsistent model deployments and difficulty tracking which model version is in production. They currently deploy models manually. Which AWS service should they implement to address these issues and prevent the anti-pattern of manual deployment without proper governance?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon SageMaker Model Registry","Amazon ECR","AWS CodeCommit","Amazon CloudWatch"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (Amazon SageMaker Model Registry) is the correct service. It provides a centralized repository to catalog models, manage their versions, track lineage, and implement approval workflows, directly addressing the anti-pattern of manual deployments without versioning or governance. Option B (Amazon ECR) stores container images, but doesn''t manage model versions or approval workflows. Option C (AWS CodeCommit) is a source control service for code, not for deployed ML models. Option D (Amazon CloudWatch) is a monitoring service, not a model management or deployment service.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  18,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_16_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_2_74',
  'Which AWS service allows developers to define their cloud infrastructure, including Amazon SageMaker resources, in a declarative way using a programming language or a markup language, facilitating automation and version control?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS CodeBuild","Amazon EventBridge","AWS CloudFormation","AWS Lambda"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (AWS CloudFormation) is the correct service. AWS CloudFormation enables you to model, provision, and manage AWS and third-party resources by treating infrastructure as code. This allows for declarative definition using JSON or YAML templates, which can be version-controlled and deployed consistently. Option A (AWS CodeBuild) is a continuous integration service. Option B (Amazon EventBridge) is an event bus for event-driven architectures. Option D (AWS Lambda) is a serverless compute service.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  19,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_16_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_2_75',
  'A data scientist has developed a custom Docker image containing specific libraries and dependencies for their machine learning model. They need a secure and scalable way to store this private image so that it can be pulled by Amazon SageMaker for training and inference. Which AWS service should they use?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon S3","AWS CodeCommit","Amazon DynamoDB","Amazon ECR"]'::json,
  '{3}',
  'Option D (Amazon ECR) is the correct service. Amazon Elastic Container Registry (ECR) is a fully managed Docker container registry that allows for secure storage and management of private Docker images. Amazon SageMaker can directly pull images from ECR for training jobs and inference endpoints. Option A (Amazon S3) is object storage and while it can store files, it''s not a managed Docker registry. Option B (AWS CodeCommit) is a source control service. Option C (Amazon DynamoDB) is a NoSQL database service.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  20,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_16_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_2_76',
  'What is the primary benefit of using Amazon SageMaker Pipelines for orchestrating machine learning workflows?',
  'mcq',
  '["It provides a visual interface for data exploration.","It automatically optimizes model hyperparameters.","It enables the creation of reproducible and auditable ML workflows.","It offers real-time monitoring of model performance."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (It enables the creation of reproducible and auditable ML workflows) is the primary benefit. Amazon SageMaker Pipelines allows you to define ML workflows as a series of steps, capturing metadata and artifacts at each stage, which ensures reproducibility, traceability, and auditability. Option A (It provides a visual interface for data exploration) is a feature of SageMaker Studio, not SageMaker Pipelines directly. Option B (It automatically optimizes model hyperparameters) is a feature of SageMaker Automatic Model Tuning, not the core function of Pipelines. Option D (It offers real-time monitoring of model performance) is handled by SageMaker Model Monitor, not Pipelines.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  21,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_16_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_2_77',
  'A machine learning team wants to ensure that every model deployed to production undergoes a formal review and approval process. They also need to maintain a clear record of which model versions are approved and deployed. Which feature of Amazon SageMaker Model Registry helps achieve this goal?',
  'mcq',
  '["Automatic model tuning","Built-in approval workflows","Real-time endpoint auto-scaling","Batch transform job scheduling"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (Built-in approval workflows) is the correct answer. Amazon SageMaker Model Registry provides built-in capabilities to define and manage approval workflows, ensuring that models meet specific criteria before being deployed to production. This helps maintain governance and quality. Option A (Automatic model tuning) is for optimizing hyperparameters. Option C (Real-time endpoint auto-scaling) is for managing inference endpoint capacity. Option D (Batch transform job scheduling) is for running batch inference jobs.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  22,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_16_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

