INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_3_50',
  'Which AWS service is used to orchestrate end-to-end machine learning workflows, including data processing, model training, and deployment steps?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon SageMaker Pipelines","AWS CodePipeline","Amazon EventBridge","AWS Step Functions"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (Amazon SageMaker Pipelines) is specifically designed for orchestrating and automating end-to-end machine learning workflows, providing steps for data processing, model training, and deployment. Option B (AWS CodePipeline) is a general-purpose CI/CD service for software releases, not specifically ML workflows. Option C (Amazon EventBridge) is an event bus service for event-driven architectures. Option D (AWS Step Functions) is a serverless workflow service that can orchestrate various AWS services, but SageMaker Pipelines is purpose-built for ML.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  72,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_16_3',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_3_51',
  'What is the primary purpose of Amazon SageMaker Model Registry?',
  'mcq',
  '["To version, manage, and approve machine learning models for deployment.","To store raw training data and processed features for model development.","To monitor the performance and health of deployed SageMaker endpoints.","To provide a centralized repository for Docker images used by SageMaker."]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (To version, manage, and approve machine learning models for deployment) accurately describes the primary purpose of Amazon SageMaker Model Registry. It provides a centralized repository for managing model versions, tracking their lineage, and facilitating approval workflows for deployment to production. Option B describes data storage services like Amazon S3. Option C describes monitoring services like Amazon CloudWatch and SageMaker Model Monitor. Option D describes Amazon ECR.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  73,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_16_3',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_3_52',
  'Which AWS service can trigger an Amazon SageMaker Pipeline execution based on a schedule, such as daily retraining, or in response to specific events?',
  'mcq',
  '["Amazon EventBridge","AWS CodeCommit","AWS CloudWatch Logs","AWS Systems Manager"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (Amazon EventBridge) is the correct service. EventBridge is a serverless event bus that makes it easy to connect applications together using data from your own applications, integrated SaaS applications, and AWS services. It can be configured to trigger SageMaker Pipelines on a schedule or in response to various events. Option B (AWS CodeCommit) is a source control service. Option C (AWS CloudWatch Logs) is for monitoring and storing logs. Option D (AWS Systems Manager) is for operational insights and management of AWS resources.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  74,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_16_3',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_3_53',
  'Which deployment strategy for machine learning models involves gradually shifting a small percentage of live traffic to a new model version to observe its performance before a full rollout?',
  'mcq',
  '["Canary release","Blue/green deployment","Rolling update","All-at-once deployment"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (Canary release) is the correct strategy. A canary release involves deploying a new version to a small subset of users or traffic, monitoring its performance, and then gradually increasing the traffic if it performs well. This minimizes risk. Option B (Blue/green deployment) involves running two identical environments (blue and green) and shifting all traffic at once. Option C (Rolling update) updates instances one by one within a single environment. Option D (All-at-once deployment) pushes the new version to all instances simultaneously, which is high risk.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  75,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_16_3',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_3_54',
  'Which AWS service is commonly used in CI/CD pipelines to build and test Docker images for machine learning models before deployment to Amazon SageMaker?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS CodeBuild","AWS CodeDeploy","AWS CodeCommit","AWS CodeStar"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (AWS CodeBuild) is a fully managed continuous integration service that compiles source code, runs tests, and produces software packages, including Docker images. It is ideal for building container images in a CI/CD pipeline. Option B (AWS CodeDeploy) automates code deployments to various compute services. Option C (AWS CodeCommit) is a source control service. Option D (AWS CodeStar) is a unified UI for developing, building, and deploying applications on AWS, integrating multiple Code services.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  76,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_16_3',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_3_55',
  'What is the primary benefit of implementing a blue/green deployment strategy for machine learning models on Amazon SageMaker?',
  'mcq',
  '["Enables zero-downtime deployments and easy rollback.","Gradually shifts traffic to the new model version.","Reduces the cost of model training and inference.","Automatically optimizes the model for different hardware."]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (Enables zero-downtime deployments and easy rollback) is the primary benefit of a blue/green deployment. It involves running two identical production environments (blue for current, green for new) and switching traffic between them. This allows for instant rollback if issues arise, with no downtime. Option B describes a canary release. Option C relates to cost optimization, not directly a deployment strategy. Option D describes SageMaker Neo.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  77,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_16_3',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_3_56',
  'Which AWS service provides a fully managed continuous delivery service that automates the release pipelines for fast and reliable application and infrastructure updates, including ML models?',
  'mcq',
  '["AWS CodePipeline","AWS CodeBuild","AWS CodeDeploy","AWS CodeCommit"]'::json,
  '{0}',
  'Option A (AWS CodePipeline) is the fully managed continuous delivery service that automates release pipelines. It orchestrates the entire release process, from source code changes through building, testing, and deploying applications, including machine learning models. Option B (AWS CodeBuild) is for building and testing code. Option C (AWS CodeDeploy) automates code deployment. Option D (AWS CodeCommit) is a source control service.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
