  'm_17_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_17_m_17_1_76',
  'An ML team has deployed a model that predicts customer churn. They notice that the model''s accuracy has been steadily declining. They suspect the characteristics of new customers are different from the training data. Which Amazon SageMaker Model Monitor capability should they focus on?',
  'mcq',
  '["Model quality monitoring","Data quality monitoring","Bias drift monitoring","Feature attribution drift monitoring"]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (Data quality monitoring) is the most relevant capability to focus on. If the characteristics of new customers (input data) are different from the training data, this indicates data drift, which is detected by data quality monitoring. While model quality will also degrade (Option A), identifying the root cause as data drift is crucial. Option C (Bias drift monitoring) and Option D (Feature attribution drift monitoring) address different aspects of model behavior.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain17_3',
  NOW(),
  63,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_17_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_17_m_17_1_77',
  'How does Amazon SageMaker Model Monitor integrate with Amazon CloudWatch Alarms for automated alerts?',
  'mcq',
  '["Model Monitor directly sends email notifications to subscribers.","Model Monitor publishes metrics to CloudWatch, which can then trigger CloudWatch Alarms.","CloudWatch Alarms directly query Model Monitor for drift detection results.","Model Monitor creates new CloudWatch metrics automatically for every drift detected."]'::json,
  '{1}',
  'Option B (Model Monitor publishes metrics to CloudWatch, which can then trigger CloudWatch Alarms) correctly describes the integration. When Amazon SageMaker Model Monitor detects drift or quality issues, it publishes relevant metrics (e.g., data quality violations, model quality scores) to Amazon CloudWatch. Users can then configure CloudWatch Alarms to monitor these specific metrics and trigger notifications or automated actions when thresholds are breached. Option A (Model Monitor directly sends email notifications) is incorrect; it uses CloudWatch for this. Option C (CloudWatch Alarms directly query Model Monitor) is incorrect; CloudWatch consumes metrics. Option D (Model Monitor creates new CloudWatch metrics automatically for every drift) is not entirely accurate; it publishes predefined metrics that reflect drift.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain17_3',
  NOW(),
  64,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_17_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_17_m_17_1_78',
  'Which of the following describes a key anti-pattern related to monitoring ML solutions?',
  'mcq',
  '["Using Amazon SageMaker Model Monitor to detect data quality issues.","Setting up Amazon CloudWatch Alarms for model quality metrics.","Only monitoring infrastructure metrics like CPU and memory utilization for a SageMaker endpoint.","Implementing triggered retraining based on drift detection."]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Only monitoring infrastructure metrics like CPU and memory utilization for a SageMaker endpoint) describes a key anti-pattern. While infrastructure metrics are important, they do not provide insight into the actual performance or behavior of the ML model itself. An endpoint can be healthy infrastructure-wise while the model''s accuracy degrades due to data drift or concept drift. ML-specific monitoring (like Amazon SageMaker Model Monitor) is required to catch model quality degradation. Options A, B, and D are all best practices for monitoring and maintaining ML solutions.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain17_3',
  NOW(),
  65,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_17_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_17_m_17_1_79',
  'A financial institution needs to ensure that their credit risk model does not develop unintended bias against specific demographic groups after deployment. Which Amazon SageMaker Model Monitor capability is most relevant?',
  'mcq',
  '["Data quality monitoring","Model quality monitoring","Bias drift monitoring","Feature attribution drift monitoring"]'::json,
  '{2}',
  'Option C (Bias drift monitoring) is most relevant for ensuring a credit risk model does not develop unintended bias against specific demographic groups. This capability specifically monitors for shifts in fairness metrics over time, helping to identify and address potential biases. Option A (Data quality monitoring) focuses on input data integrity. Option B (Model quality monitoring) tracks overall performance. Option D (Feature attribution drift monitoring) tracks changes in feature importance.',
