  '{0,2,3}',
  'Option A (SMOTE) is a technique to generate synthetic samples for the minority class. Option C (Oversampling) involves duplicating samples from the minority class. Option D (Undersampling) involves reducing the number of samples from the majority class. All three are effective strategies for handling class imbalance. Option B (Normalization) and Option E (Feature scaling) are techniques for scaling numerical features, not for addressing class imbalance.',
