  'Option B (AWS Glue) is a serverless data integration service that enables users to perform ETL operations, including data quality checks and transformations, as part of a data pipeline. Option C (AWS Glue DataBrew) is a visual data preparation tool that allows users to clean, normalize, and validate data without writing code, making it suitable for data quality checks. Option A (Amazon S3) is for storage, not active data quality checks. Option D (Amazon Kinesis Data Streams) is for real-time ingestion. Option E (Amazon Redshift) is a data warehouse for analytical querying, not primarily for ETL or data quality checks.',
