  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (Amazon SageMaker Clarify) is used to detect potential bias in machine learning models and training data. It helps identify bias related to sensitive attributes before model training, which is crucial for ethical AI (anti-pattern ap-1.3-002). Option B (Amazon SageMaker Ground Truth) is a data labeling service that helps you build highly accurate training datasets for machine learning. It provides human-in-the-loop workflows to label various data types. Option C (AWS Glue Data Catalog) is a metadata repository. Option D (Amazon Athena) is a query service for S3 data. Option E (Amazon Redshift) is a data warehouse. None of these are designed for bias detection or data labeling.',
