) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_14_m_14_3_131',
  'A data science team wants to track the lineage of their machine learning models, including data sources, processing steps, and model versions, for auditing and reproducibility. Which AWS services can help establish data versioning and lineage? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Amazon S3 Versioning","Amazon SageMaker ML Lineage Tracking","AWS CloudTrail","Amazon DynamoDB","AWS Config"]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (Amazon S3 Versioning) helps maintain multiple versions of an object in an Amazon S3 bucket, allowing for recovery from accidental deletions or overwrites, which is a fundamental aspect of data versioning for raw and processed datasets. Option B (Amazon SageMaker ML Lineage Tracking) automatically tracks the lineage of ML workflows, including data sources, processing jobs, training jobs, and model artifacts. This provides an end-to-end view of how a model was built, crucial for reproducibility and auditing. Option C (AWS CloudTrail) records API calls and related events, useful for auditing actions but not for tracking data or model lineage itself. Option D (Amazon DynamoDB) is a NoSQL database, not designed for ML lineage tracking. Option E (AWS Config) assesses, audits, and evaluates the configurations of AWS resources, not the lineage of ML data or models.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain14_3',
  NOW(),
  82,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_14_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_14_m_14_3_132',
  'Before training a critical machine learning model, a company needs to perform comprehensive data quality checks to ensure completeness, consistency, and accuracy of the dataset. Which AWS services are best suited for automating these data quality checks? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["AWS Glue","Amazon SageMaker Data Wrangler","Amazon S3","Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose","Amazon Redshift"]'::json,
  '{0,1}',
  'Option A (AWS Glue) provides AWS Glue Data Quality, which allows you to define, monitor, and manage data quality rules for your data lake and data warehouses. It can automatically evaluate data quality and take actions based on predefined rules. Option B (Amazon SageMaker Data Wrangler) offers built-in data quality and insights reports that can detect issues like missing values, outliers, and data type mismatches, helping to ensure data integrity before feature engineering and modeling. Option C (Amazon S3) is a storage service and does not inherently perform data quality checks. Option D (Amazon Kinesis Data Firehose) is for data ingestion, not quality validation. Option E (Amazon Redshift) is a data warehouse that can store data, but its primary function is not automated data quality checks.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain14_3',
  NOW(),
  83,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_14_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_14_m_14_3_133',
  'A machine learning team is working with a new dataset and needs to ensure its quality before training. Which aspects are typically checked as part of data quality assessment for machine learning? (Select THREE.)',
