  '{0,2}',
  'Option A (Amazon SageMaker Clarify) is specifically designed to detect and measure bias in training data and models. It can identify disparities in data based on sensitive attributes, which is crucial for building fair ML models (anti-pattern ap-1.3-002). Option C (AWS Glue DataBrew) is a visual data preparation tool that can be used to profile data and identify potential issues, including distributions that might indicate bias, although Clarify is more specialized for bias detection. Option B (Amazon SageMaker Ground Truth) is for data labeling. Option D (Amazon S3) is for storage. Option E (AWS Lake Formation) is for building secure data lakes. These services do not directly detect or quantify bias in the training data.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain14_3',
  NOW(),
  86,
