  'The scenario describes overfitting. Option C (Implement L2 regularization) and Option E (Apply early stopping) are effective and often faster/cheaper first responses to overfitting. L2 regularization penalizes large weights, discouraging complex models, while early stopping halts training when validation performance degrades. Option A (Increase the number of training epochs) would likely worsen overfitting. Option B (Use a more complex model architecture) would also exacerbate overfitting. Option D (Collect significantly more training data) can help, but it is often a more time-consuming and expensive solution, and not usually the first technique to try.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain15_3',
  NOW(),
  6,
