  'What are common operational metrics provided by Amazon CloudWatch for SageMaker endpoints that help in assessing the endpoint''s health and performance? (Select THREE.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Invocations","ModelLatency","InvocationError","BiasDrift","DataQualityViolations"]'::json,
  '{0,1,2}',
  'Option A (Invocations) tracks the number of successful calls to the endpoint, indicating throughput. Option B (ModelLatency) measures the processing time for requests, indicating performance. Option C (InvocationError) counts failed requests, indicating endpoint health and reliability issues. Option D (BiasDrift) and Option E (DataQualityViolations) are metrics provided by Amazon SageMaker Model Monitor, which focus on model-specific quality and data integrity, rather than general operational health and performance metrics directly from the endpoint infrastructure.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain17_3',
  NOW(),
  16,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_17_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_17_m_17_2_109',
  'Which actions can be taken to optimize the cost of Amazon SageMaker training jobs that are not time-critical and can tolerate flexible completion times? (Select TWO.)',
  'multiple',
  '["Using Amazon EC2 Spot Instances for training jobs","Implementing distributed training with multiple GPU instances","Configuring SageMaker Model Monitor for training data","Selecting the smallest possible instance type that meets performance needs","Enabling SageMaker Debugger for real-time profiling"]'::json,
  '{0,3}',
  'Option A (Using Amazon EC2 Spot Instances for training jobs) is a highly effective way to reduce training costs for non-critical jobs, as Spot Instances offer significant discounts. Option D (Selecting the smallest possible instance type that meets performance needs) is a fundamental right-sizing strategy that directly reduces compute costs. Option B (Implementing distributed training with multiple GPU instances) typically increases costs, although it can reduce training time for large models. Option C (Configuring SageMaker Model Monitor for training data) is for data quality and drift detection, not cost optimization of the training job itself. Option E (Enabling SageMaker Debugger for real-time profiling) is for debugging and optimizing model training, which might indirectly save costs by reducing failed runs, but it''s not a primary cost optimization mechanism for the compute resources.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain17_3',
  NOW(),
  17,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_17_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

