  'Option B (Amazon CloudWatch) is used to collect and track metrics, collect and monitor log files, and set alarms for your AWS resources, including Amazon SageMaker endpoints. Option C (Amazon SageMaker Model Monitor) specifically monitors the quality of ML models in production, detecting data quality, model quality, bias, and feature attribution drift. Option A (AWS CloudTrail) records API calls and related events, primarily for auditing and governance, not operational health. Option D (AWS Config) assesses, audits, and evaluates the configurations of your AWS resources. Option E (Amazon S3) is object storage and not a monitoring service.',
