VALUES (
  'q_15_m_15_3_123',
  'A data scientist has trained a new model using Amazon SageMaker and observes poor performance on unseen data. Order the typical steps to diagnose and address potential overfitting in the model.',
  'ordering',
  '["Evaluate the model''s performance on both the training and a separate validation dataset using appropriate metrics.","Analyze the training and validation loss curves to identify divergence, indicating overfitting.","Implement regularization techniques (e.g., L1, L2, dropout) or early stopping during training.","Adjust model complexity by reducing the number of layers or parameters, or consider collecting more diverse data if regularization is insufficient."]'::json,
  '{0,1,2,3}',
  'Option A (correct) is the initial diagnostic step to understand how the model performs on known vs. unknown data. Option B (correct) provides visual evidence of overfitting by comparing loss trends. Option C (correct) is a common and effective first response to overfitting, often faster and cheaper than collecting more data. Option D (correct) is a subsequent step if regularization is not enough, involving more significant model architecture changes or data acquisition. This sequence represents a logical progression for addressing overfitting.',
