VALUES (
  'q_15_m_15_2_126',
  'A team is developing a new deep learning model with a large number of parameters and needs to train it efficiently. Order the steps to configure distributed training using Amazon SageMaker.',
  'ordering',
  '["Prepare the training script to support distributed training, often using frameworks like Horovod or SageMaker''s distributed data/model parallelism libraries.","Select multiple Amazon EC2 GPU instances suitable for deep learning workloads (e.g., p3, p4, g5).","Configure the SageMaker Training Job to use the distributed training strategy (e.g., data parallelism, model parallelism).","Launch the SageMaker Training Job and monitor the resource utilization and model convergence."]'::json,
  '{0,1,2,3}',
  'Option A (correct) is foundational, as the training script must be designed to handle distributed operations. Option B (correct) involves provisioning the necessary hardware for parallel processing. Option C (correct) explicitly tells SageMaker how to distribute the workload. Option D (correct) is the execution and monitoring phase. This order ensures the software, hardware, and configuration are all aligned for effective distributed training.',
