  '{0,1,2,3}',
  'Option A (correct) is the foundational step for any k-fold cross-validation. Option B (correct) defines the iterative process of using different data splits. Option C (correct) describes the core training and evaluation loop for each iteration. Option D (correct) is the final step to synthesize the results from all iterations into a single, robust performance estimate. This order outlines the standard procedure for cross-validation.',
