INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_15_m_15_2_130',
  'A machine learning engineer is setting up a new training job on Amazon SageMaker for a large dataset. They want to reduce training costs by leveraging Spot Instances while ensuring job resilience. Order the steps to configure SageMaker Managed Spot Training.',
  'ordering',
  '["Set the `use_spot_instances` parameter to `True` in the SageMaker Estimator configuration.","Specify a `max_wait_time_in_seconds` to define how long SageMaker should wait for Spot Instances.","Enable checkpointing in the training script to save model state periodically.","Launch the SageMaker Training Job."]'::json,
  '{2,0,1,3}',
  'To ensure job resilience with Spot Instances, checkpointing is critical. Option C (Enable checkpointing in the training script to save model state periodically) allows the job to resume from the last saved state if interrupted. Next, Option A (Set the `use_spot_instances` parameter to `True` in the SageMaker Estimator configuration) explicitly tells SageMaker to use Spot Instances. Option B (Specify a `max_wait_time_in_seconds` to define how long SageMaker should wait for Spot Instances) configures the waiting behavior for Spot Instances. Finally, Option D (Launch the SageMaker Training Job) starts the training process with the configured Spot Instance settings, addressing anti-pattern [ap-2.2-002].',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain15_3',
  NOW(),
  53,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_15_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_15_m_15_2_131',
  'A data science team is developing a new model and needs to find the optimal hyperparameters to maximize its performance. Order the steps to effectively use Amazon SageMaker Automatic Model Tuning (HPO) for this task.',
  'ordering',
  '["Define the hyperparameter ranges and the objective metric (e.g., accuracy, F1-score) to optimize.","Launch the SageMaker HPO job, specifying the estimator, objective, and search strategy.","Analyze the HPO job results to identify the best performing hyperparameter combination.","Prepare a SageMaker Estimator for the training job, including the training script and instance types."]'::json,
  '{3,0,1,2}',
  'Before starting an HPO job, the training environment needs to be defined. Option D (Prepare a SageMaker Estimator for the training job, including the training script and instance types) sets up the base training job. Next, Option A (Define the hyperparameter ranges and the objective metric (e.g., accuracy, F1-score) to optimize) specifies what HPO should search for and how to evaluate it. Then, Option B (Launch the SageMaker HPO job, specifying the estimator, objective, and search strategy) initiates the tuning process. Finally, Option C (Analyze the HPO job results to identify the best performing hyperparameter combination) allows the team to select the best model, avoiding anti-pattern [ap-2.2-001] by having well-defined ranges and objectives.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain15_3',
  NOW(),
  54,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_15_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_15_m_15_2_132',
  'A machine learning engineer needs to train a large deep learning model using a custom PyTorch script on Amazon SageMaker. Order the steps to configure and launch a SageMaker Training Job for this scenario.',
  'ordering',
  '["Upload the training dataset to an Amazon S3 bucket.","Create a SageMaker PyTorch Estimator, specifying the entry point script, instance type, and S3 input data.","Define the custom PyTorch training script, including model definition, data loading, and training loop.","Call the `fit()` method on the Estimator to start the training job."]'::json,
  '{2,0,1,3}',
  'The core of custom training is the script itself. Option A (Define the custom PyTorch training script, including model definition, data loading, and training loop) is the first logical step. Next, Option B (Upload the training dataset to an Amazon S3 bucket) makes the data accessible to SageMaker. Then, Option C (Create a SageMaker PyTorch Estimator, specifying the entry point script, instance type, and S3 input data) configures the training environment. Finally, Option D (Call the `fit()` method on the Estimator to start the training job) launches the training process.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain15_3',
  NOW(),
  55,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_15_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_15_m_15_2_133',
  'A data scientist is observing overfitting in their model during training. To address this, they decide to implement regularization techniques. Order the steps to apply regularization effectively.',
  'ordering',
  '["Monitor the model''s performance on a validation set during training.","Add L1 or L2 regularization terms to the model''s loss function.","Introduce dropout layers into the neural network architecture.","Adjust the regularization strength (e.g., lambda for L1/L2, dropout rate) based on validation performance."]'::json,
  '{1,2,0,3}',
  'Regularization involves modifying the model or training process. Option B (Add L1 or L2 regularization terms to the model''s loss function) is a common way to penalize large weights. Simultaneously, Option C (Introduce dropout layers into the neural network architecture) can be applied to randomly drop units during training, preventing co-adaptation. After implementing these, Option A (Monitor the model''s performance on a validation set during training) is crucial to observe the effect of regularization. Finally, Option D (Adjust the regularization strength (e.g., lambda for L1/L2, dropout rate) based on validation performance) fine-tunes the regularization to achieve optimal balance, aligning with the approach to address overfitting before collecting more data [ap-2.3-001].',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain15_3',
  NOW(),
  56,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_15_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_15_m_15_2_134',
  'A team is training a large language model and needs to distribute the training workload across multiple GPU instances to speed up the process. Order the steps to set up distributed training on Amazon SageMaker.',
  'ordering',
  '["Configure the SageMaker Estimator with the desired number of instances and instance types (e.g., EC2 GPU instances).","Prepare the training script to handle distributed data loading and model synchronization.","Launch the SageMaker Training Job.","Choose a distributed training strategy, such as data parallelism or model parallelism, based on model size and data volume."]'::json,
  '{1,3,0,2}',
  'The foundation of distributed training is a script capable of handling it. Option B (Prepare the training script to handle distributed data loading and model synchronization) ensures the code is ready. Next, Option D (Choose a distributed training strategy, such as data parallelism or model parallelism, based on model size and data volume) determines how the workload will be split. With the script and strategy in mind, Option A (Configure the SageMaker Estimator with the desired number of instances and instance types (e.g., EC2 GPU instances)) sets up the SageMaker environment. Finally, Option C (Launch the SageMaker Training Job) initiates the distributed training.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain15_3',
  NOW(),
  57,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_15_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_15_m_15_2_135',
  'A data scientist is performing hyperparameter tuning for a new model and wants to use cross-validation to ensure robust evaluation of different hyperparameter combinations. Order the steps to integrate cross-validation into the tuning process.',
  'ordering',
  '["Split the training dataset into multiple folds (e.g., K-folds).","Train the model on K-1 folds and evaluate on the remaining fold for each hyperparameter combination.","Average the performance metrics across all folds for each hyperparameter combination.","Select the hyperparameter combination that yields the best average performance."]'::json,
  '{0,1,2,3}',
  'Cross-validation begins with dividing the data. Option A (Split the training dataset into multiple folds (e.g., K-folds)) creates the necessary partitions. Next, Option B (Train the model on K-1 folds and evaluate on the remaining fold for each hyperparameter combination) executes the iterative training and evaluation process for each fold. After all folds are processed, Option C (Average the performance metrics across all folds for each hyperparameter combination) aggregates the results to get a more stable performance estimate. Finally, Option D (Select the hyperparameter combination that yields the best average performance) uses these averaged metrics to choose the optimal hyperparameters.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain15_3',
  NOW(),
  58,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_15_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

