  '{3,2,0,1}',
  'A typical CI/CD pipeline for SageMaker models using AWS CodePipeline starts with the Source stage (Option D), where code changes are detected (e.g., in CodeCommit). This triggers the Build stage (Option C), where artifacts like Docker images for inference are created (e.g., using CodeBuild). After a successful build, the Model registration stage (Option A) is typically used to register the new model version in SageMaker Model Registry. Finally, the Deploy stage (Option B) updates the SageMaker endpoint with the new model version, often incorporating canary or blue/green strategies.',
