INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_3_102',
  'After defining all necessary steps for an Amazon SageMaker Pipeline, an MLOps engineer needs to initiate its execution. Order the actions to successfully run a defined SageMaker Pipeline.',
  'ordering',
  '["Monitor the pipeline execution status and logs.","Define the SageMaker Pipeline object with its steps.","Start the pipeline execution using `pipeline.start()`.","Prepare input data and artifacts in Amazon S3."]'::json,
  '{3,1,2,0}',
  'Running a SageMaker Pipeline requires data and a defined pipeline. Option D (Prepare input data and artifacts in Amazon S3) ensures all necessary inputs are ready. Next, Option B (Define the SageMaker Pipeline object) constructs the pipeline with its steps. Then, Option C (Start the pipeline execution) initiates the workflow. Finally, Option A (Monitor the pipeline execution status and logs) is essential to track progress and troubleshoot.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  47,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_16_3',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_3_103',
  'A team wants to deploy a new model version to a SageMaker endpoint using a canary release strategy to minimize risk. Order the steps for implementing a canary deployment.',
  'ordering',
  '["Gradually shift more traffic to the new model variant.","Deploy the new model version to a new endpoint variant with a small percentage of traffic.","Monitor the performance and metrics of the new model variant.","Fully shift all traffic to the new model variant and decommission the old one."]'::json,
  '{1,2,0,3}',
  'A canary deployment starts with a cautious rollout. Option B (Deploy the new model version to a new endpoint variant with a small percentage of traffic) introduces the new model to a small user base. Next, Option C (Monitor the performance and metrics) is crucial to assess its stability and performance. If satisfactory, Option A (Gradually shift more traffic) increases exposure. Finally, Option D (Fully shift all traffic and decommission the old one) completes the rollout once confidence is high.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  48,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_16_3',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_3_104',
  'To automate the triggering of an Amazon SageMaker Pipeline based on a specific event, an engineer decides to use Amazon EventBridge. Order the steps to set up an EventBridge rule for this purpose.',
  'ordering',
  '["Define the SageMaker Pipeline to be triggered.","Create an EventBridge rule with an event pattern or schedule.","Configure the EventBridge rule''s target to invoke the SageMaker Pipeline.","Ensure the EventBridge execution role has permissions to start SageMaker Pipelines."]'::json,
  '{0,1,2,3}',
  'Setting up an EventBridge trigger for a SageMaker Pipeline requires the pipeline to exist first. Option A (Define the SageMaker Pipeline) is the prerequisite. Next, Option B (Create an EventBridge rule) defines the trigger condition. Then, Option C (Configure the EventBridge rule''s target) specifies that the pipeline should be invoked. Finally, Option D (Ensure the EventBridge execution role has permissions) is a critical security step for the rule to function.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  49,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_16_3',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_3_105',
  'A machine learning model needs to be retrained weekly to incorporate new data. An MLOps engineer wants to automate this process. Order the steps to set up automated retraining on a schedule.',
  'ordering',
  '["Define a SageMaker Pipeline that includes training and model registration steps.","Configure an Amazon EventBridge rule with a scheduled trigger (e.g., cron expression).","Set the EventBridge rule''s target to start the SageMaker Pipeline.","Monitor the pipeline executions and model performance."]'::json,
  '{0,1,2,3}',
  'Automating model retraining on a schedule begins with the retraining workflow itself. Option A (Define a SageMaker Pipeline) encapsulates the training and registration logic. Next, Option B (Configure an Amazon EventBridge rule with a scheduled trigger) sets up the recurring schedule. Then, Option C (Set the EventBridge rule''s target) links the schedule to the pipeline. Finally, Option D (Monitor the pipeline executions and model performance) is essential for operational oversight.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  50,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_16_3',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_3_106',
  'For a critical production ML endpoint, a blue/green deployment strategy is chosen to ensure zero downtime during model updates. Order the steps to perform a blue/green deployment on a SageMaker endpoint.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create a new ''Green'' endpoint with the new model version.","Gradually shift traffic from the ''Blue'' endpoint to the ''Green'' endpoint.","Monitor the ''Green'' endpoint''s performance.","Decommission the old ''Blue'' endpoint after successful traffic shift."]'::json,
  '{0,1,2,3}',
  'A blue/green deployment strategy ensures a new version is fully tested before replacing the old one. Option A (Create a new ''Green'' endpoint) provisions the new environment. Next, Option B (Gradually shift traffic) directs users to the new endpoint. Option C (Monitor the ''Green'' endpoint''s performance) is critical during the traffic shift. Finally, Option D (Decommission the old ''Blue'' endpoint) removes the old environment once the new one is stable and fully serving traffic.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  51,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_16_3',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_3_107',
  'An ML engineer is designing a SageMaker Pipeline where a subsequent step should only execute if a condition is met (e.g., model accuracy above a threshold). Order the components for defining such a conditional step.',
  'ordering',
  '["Define a `ConditionStep` that evaluates a condition (e.g., `ComparisonCondition`).","Define the steps to be executed if the condition is true.","Define the steps to be executed if the condition is false.","Add the `ConditionStep` to the SageMaker Pipeline definition."]'::json,
  '{1,2,0,3}',
  'When defining a conditional step in SageMaker Pipelines, the branches must be defined first. Option B (Define the steps to be executed if the condition is true) and Option C (Define the steps to be executed if the condition is false) specify the alternative paths. Next, Option A (Define a `ConditionStep`) encapsulates the logic for evaluating the condition and referencing these branches. Finally, Option D (Add the `ConditionStep` to the SageMaker Pipeline definition) integrates it into the overall pipeline.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  52,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_16_3',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_3_108',
  'A retail company wants to automatically retrain its recommendation model if data drift is detected in its input features. Order the steps to implement an automated retraining workflow triggered by data drift.',
  'ordering',
  '["Configure a data quality monitoring job in SageMaker Model Monitor.","Define a SageMaker Pipeline for model retraining and deployment.","Set up an Amazon EventBridge rule to trigger the pipeline on data drift alerts.","Establish a baseline for data quality metrics."]'::json,
  '{1,3,0,2}',
  'Implementing an automated retraining workflow triggered by data drift starts with defining the retraining process. Option B (Define a SageMaker Pipeline) outlines the retraining and deployment steps. Next, Option D (Establish a baseline for data quality metrics) provides a reference for detecting drift. Then, Option A (Configure a data quality monitoring job in SageMaker Model Monitor) continuously checks for drift. Finally, Option C (Set up an Amazon EventBridge rule) connects drift alerts to trigger the retraining pipeline.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  53,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_16_3',
  'easy'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_3_109',
  'Order the basic steps to create and execute a SageMaker Pipeline for an automated ML workflow.',
  'ordering',
  '["Start pipeline execution","Monitor pipeline run and status","Define pipeline steps and their dependencies","Create the SageMaker Pipeline"]'::json,
  '{2,3,0,1}',
  'To create and execute a SageMaker Pipeline, the first step is to Define the pipeline steps and their dependencies (Option C), outlining the sequence of operations like processing, training, and evaluation. Next, the SageMaker Pipeline is Created (Option D) based on this definition. Once created, the pipeline execution is Started (Option A) to initiate the workflow. Finally, the pipeline run and status are Monitored (Option B) to track progress and identify any issues.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  54,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_16_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_3_110',
  'An MLOps team at a large technology company aims to automate their entire machine learning workflow, from data preprocessing and feature engineering to model training, evaluation, and registration. They want to use Amazon SageMaker Pipelines to orchestrate these steps, ensuring reproducibility and governance for their critical models. The goal is to create a robust, automated continuous training pipeline.',
  'ordering',
  '["Define a data processing step using SageMaker Processing jobs.","Define a model evaluation step to assess model performance.","Define a model training step using SageMaker Training jobs.","Define a model registration step to add the approved model to SageMaker Model Registry.","Create and execute the SageMaker Pipeline definition."]'::json,
  '{0,2,1,3,4}',
  'Setting up a SageMaker Pipeline for continuous training involves defining the logical flow of ML operations. Option A (Define a data processing step) is the natural starting point, as data preparation typically precedes training. Option C (Define a model training step) follows, using the processed data to train the model. Option B (Define a model evaluation step) is crucial next, as it assesses the quality of the trained model. Option D (Define a model registration step) is performed after evaluation, adding the model to the SageMaker Model Registry for versioning and approval. Finally, Option E (Create and execute the SageMaker Pipeline definition) orchestrates all these defined steps into an automated workflow. This sequence ensures a logical progression from data to a registered model.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  55,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_16_3',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_3_111',
  'A critical production model for an online gaming platform needs to be updated with a new version. To minimize the risk of service disruption and ensure the new model performs as expected in a live environment, the MLOps team decides to implement a canary deployment strategy. This allows for gradual traffic shifting and monitoring before a full rollout.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create a new SageMaker endpoint configuration with two production variants: the old model (95% traffic) and the new model (5% traffic).","Monitor the performance metrics (e.g., error rate, latency) of the new model variant.","Create a new SageMaker Model resource for the updated model version.","Gradually shift more traffic to the new model variant based on satisfactory performance.","Update the SageMaker endpoint to use the new endpoint configuration."]'::json,
  '{2,0,4,1,3}',
  'Implementing a canary deployment involves preparing the new model, configuring traffic distribution, and then gradually shifting traffic. Option C (Create a new SageMaker Model resource for the updated model version) is the initial step, as the new model must be registered. Option A (Create a new SageMaker endpoint configuration with two production variants) defines how traffic will be split between the old and new models, with a small percentage directed to the new canary. Option E (Update the SageMaker endpoint to use the new endpoint configuration) applies this configuration, initiating the canary release. Option B (Monitor the performance metrics) is crucial during the canary phase to detect any regressions. Finally, Option D (Gradually shift more traffic to the new model variant) is performed iteratively as confidence in the new model grows, preventing the anti-pattern [ap-3.3-001] of deploying directly to 100% traffic.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  56,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_16_3',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_3_112',
  'An ML team wants to automatically retrain their recommendation model whenever new customer interaction data is uploaded to a specific Amazon S3 bucket. This ensures the model stays up-to-date without manual intervention. They decide to use Amazon EventBridge to trigger a pre-defined Amazon SageMaker Pipeline for retraining. The MLOps team needs to set up this event-driven automation.',
  'ordering',
  '["Configure Amazon S3 event notifications to publish events to Amazon EventBridge when new data arrives.","Create an Amazon EventBridge rule that filters for the S3 event and specifies the SageMaker Pipeline as a target.","Define and create the Amazon SageMaker Pipeline for model retraining.","Test the automated trigger by uploading new data to the S3 bucket."]'::json,
  '{2,0,1,3}',
  'To trigger a SageMaker Pipeline using Amazon EventBridge based on S3 events, the pipeline must exist first, followed by the event source and rule. Option C (Define and create the Amazon SageMaker Pipeline for model retraining) is the foundational step, as the pipeline must be available to be triggered. Option A (Configure Amazon S3 event notifications) sets up the source of the event, ensuring that S3 sends notifications when new data is uploaded. Option B (Create an Amazon EventBridge rule) then defines the logic to capture these S3 events and directs them to the SageMaker Pipeline. Finally, Option D (Test the automated trigger) verifies that the entire setup functions as expected. This sequence ensures that the pipeline is ready before the trigger mechanism is configured.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  57,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_16_3',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_3_113',
  'An MLOps team is implementing a robust CI/CD pipeline for their ML models, aiming for strong governance, version control, and approval workflows. They want to integrate Amazon SageMaker Model Registry into their pipeline to manage model versions and ensure only approved models are deployed to production. This requires a structured process for model lifecycle management.',
  'ordering',
  '["Configure the CI/CD pipeline to retrieve the latest approved model version from SageMaker Model Registry for deployment.","Train and evaluate the machine learning model within a SageMaker Pipeline or other automated process.","Register the evaluated model in Amazon SageMaker Model Registry, including performance metrics and lineage.","Define an approval status (e.g., ''Approved'') in the SageMaker Model Registry for production deployment."]'::json,
  '{1,2,3,0}',
  'Integrating SageMaker Model Registry into a CI/CD pipeline involves a sequence from model creation to deployment approval. Option B (Train and evaluate the machine learning model) is the initial step, as a model must be ready for registration. Option C (Register the evaluated model in Amazon SageMaker Model Registry) then adds the model, its metrics, and lineage to the registry for versioning. Option D (Define an approval status) is crucial for governance, ensuring that only models meeting specific criteria are marked for production. Finally, Option A (Configure the CI/CD pipeline to retrieve the latest approved model version) automates the deployment process, pulling only models that have passed the approval gates. This prevents the anti-pattern [ap-3.2-001] of manually deploying models without a model registry or approval workflow.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  58,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_16_3',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_3_114',
  'A development team at a financial technology company needs to establish a fully automated CI/CD pipeline for their machine learning models. The pipeline should handle source code management, model packaging, and deployment to Amazon SageMaker, ensuring rapid and reliable delivery of new model versions to production. They plan to use AWS CodePipeline and AWS CodeBuild.',
  'ordering',
  '["Configure an AWS CodeBuild project for model packaging, containerization, and testing.","Store the ML model''s source code and Dockerfile in an AWS CodeCommit repository.","Define the SageMaker deployment steps (e.g., create model, endpoint configuration, endpoint) within the pipeline.","Create an AWS CodePipeline with source, build, and deploy stages.","Trigger the CodePipeline manually or automatically upon code changes."]'::json,
  '{1,0,3,2,4}',
  'Setting up an AWS CodePipeline for ML model deployment requires a clear sequence of defining components and stages. Option B (Store the ML model''s source code and Dockerfile in an AWS CodeCommit repository) is the initial source stage. Option A (Configure an AWS CodeBuild project) is the build stage, responsible for preparing the model and its container. Option D (Create an AWS CodePipeline with source, build, and deploy stages) then orchestrates these stages. Option C (Define the SageMaker deployment steps) specifies the actions CodePipeline will take in the deploy stage to provision SageMaker resources. Finally, Option E (Trigger the CodePipeline) initiates the automated workflow. This ensures that the source, build, and deploy components are in place before the pipeline is activated.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  59,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_16_3',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_3_115',
  'A large social media company needs to update its content moderation model deployed on Amazon SageMaker. To ensure zero downtime and allow for extensive testing of the new model version in a production-like environment before switching all live traffic, the MLOps team decides to implement a blue/green deployment strategy. This approach minimizes risk and provides a quick rollback mechanism.',
  'ordering',
  '["Deploy the new model version to a ''Green'' SageMaker endpoint, separate from the ''Blue'' (current production) endpoint.","Perform extensive integration and performance testing on the ''Green'' endpoint.","Update the client applications or load balancer to direct all traffic to the ''Green'' endpoint.","Decommission the ''Blue'' (old) endpoint after successful traffic cutover and monitoring.","Monitor the ''Green'' endpoint''s performance and stability after traffic switch."]'::json,
  '{0,1,2,4,3}',
  'A blue/green deployment strategy for SageMaker endpoints involves deploying a new environment, testing it, and then switching traffic. Option A (Deploy the new model version to a ''Green'' SageMaker endpoint) is the first step, creating the new, isolated environment. Option B (Perform extensive integration and performance testing on the ''Green'' endpoint) is critical to validate the new version before exposing it to live traffic. Option C (Update the client applications or load balancer to direct all traffic to the ''Green'' endpoint) is the cutover step, switching live traffic. Option E (Monitor the ''Green'' endpoint''s performance and stability) is essential immediately after the switch to ensure the new endpoint handles production load. Finally, Option D (Decommission the ''Blue'' (old) endpoint) is done after confirming the ''Green'' endpoint is stable, freeing up resources. This strategy prevents the anti-pattern [ap-3.3-001] of directly deploying to 100% traffic without thorough validation.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  60,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_16_3',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_3_116',
  'A predictive maintenance model used by an industrial manufacturer shows signs of performance degradation over time due to changes in sensor data distribution (data drift). The MLOps team wants to automate the retraining process to ensure the model''s accuracy remains high. They decide to use Amazon SageMaker Model Monitor to detect drift and Amazon EventBridge to trigger a retraining pipeline.',
  'ordering',
  '["Configure Amazon EventBridge to capture data drift events from SageMaker Model Monitor.","Set up Amazon SageMaker Model Monitor to continuously analyze inference data for data drift.","Create a SageMaker Pipeline for automated model retraining.","Configure an EventBridge rule to trigger the retraining pipeline upon drift detection.","Monitor the model''s performance and retraining pipeline executions."]'::json,
  '{2,1,0,3,4}',
  'Automating retraining based on data drift requires establishing the retraining mechanism, then the detection, and finally the trigger. Option C (Create a SageMaker Pipeline for automated model retraining) is the foundational step, as the retraining process itself must be defined. Option B (Set up Amazon SageMaker Model Monitor) is next, as it''s responsible for detecting the data drift. Option A (Configure Amazon EventBridge to capture data drift events) enables EventBridge to receive notifications from Model Monitor. Option D (Configure an EventBridge rule to trigger the retraining pipeline) then links the drift event to the retraining pipeline, automating the process. Finally, Option E (Monitor the model''s performance and retraining pipeline executions) is crucial for validating the effectiveness of the automated system. This ensures the retraining mechanism is ready before the drift detection and triggering are configured.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  61,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_16_3',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_3_117',
  'A data science team is developing a new credit risk assessment model. The model''s deployment strategy depends on its performance during evaluation: if it meets a certain accuracy threshold, it should be registered in the model registry; otherwise, a notification should be sent for manual review. The MLOps team wants to implement this conditional logic using Amazon SageMaker Pipelines to automate the workflow.',
  'ordering',
  '["Define a `ConditionStep` in the pipeline based on the evaluation metrics.","Define a training step to train the credit risk model.","Define a model registration step to register the model if the condition is met.","Define an evaluation step to assess the trained model''s performance and capture metrics.","Execute the SageMaker Pipeline to apply the conditional logic."]'::json,
  '{1,3,0,2,4}',
  'Defining a SageMaker Pipeline with conditional steps requires a logical flow from training to evaluation and then decision-making. Option B (Define a training step) is the initial step, as a model must be trained. Option D (Define an evaluation step) follows, assessing the trained model''s performance and generating metrics. Option A (Define a `ConditionStep`) is the crucial step for conditional logic, which uses the metrics from the evaluation step to determine the next action. Option C (Define a model registration step) is one of the potential subsequent steps, executed if the condition is met (e.g., accuracy threshold passed). Option E (Execute the SageMaker Pipeline) initiates the entire workflow, including the conditional branching. This sequence ensures that the model is trained and evaluated before any conditional decisions are made.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  62,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_16_3',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_3_118',
  'An MLOps team wants to set up a continuous integration and continuous deployment (CI/CD) pipeline for their machine learning models using AWS CodePipeline and SageMaker. Order the essential steps to achieve this.',
  'ordering',
  '["Configure a CodePipeline stage for model deployment to SageMaker.","Set up a source stage in CodePipeline to detect changes in a Git repository.","Integrate AWS CodeBuild to build and test the model artifact.","Define a SageMaker Pipeline for model training and registration."]'::json,
  '{1,2,3,0}',
  'Option B (Set up a source stage in CodePipeline to detect changes in a Git repository) is the initial step for any CI/CD pipeline, triggering the workflow upon code changes. Option C (Integrate AWS CodeBuild to build and test the model artifact) typically follows the source stage for compiling code and running unit tests. Option D (Define a SageMaker Pipeline for model training and registration) represents the ML-specific part of the CI/CD, where the model is trained, evaluated, and registered. Finally, Option A (Configure a CodePipeline stage for model deployment to SageMaker) handles the actual deployment of the registered model to a SageMaker endpoint.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  63,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_16_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_3_119',
  'A company wants to deploy a new version of a machine learning model to a SageMaker endpoint with minimal risk, using a canary release strategy. Order the steps to implement this deployment approach.',
  'ordering',
  '["Monitor the performance of the new model version with a small percentage of traffic.","Create a new SageMaker endpoint configuration with the updated model version.","Shift a small percentage of inference traffic to the new model variant.","Gradually increase traffic to the new model variant and eventually remove the old variant."]'::json,
  '{1,2,0,3}',
  'Option B (Create a new SageMaker endpoint configuration with the updated model version) is the first step, as it defines the new model to be deployed. Option C (Shift a small percentage of inference traffic to the new model variant) initiates the canary release by directing a small portion of requests to the new model. Option A (Monitor the performance of the new model version with a small percentage of traffic) is crucial to validate the new model''s behavior and performance without impacting all users. Finally, Option D (Gradually increase traffic to the new model variant and eventually remove the old variant) represents the full rollout once the canary phase confirms stability and performance.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  64,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_16_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

