INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_17_m_17_2_131',
  'An ML team wants to implement Amazon SageMaker Model Monitor to detect data quality issues on a production endpoint. Order the steps required to set up this monitoring solution.',
  'ordering',
  '["Generate a baseline for model data","Configure data capture on the SageMaker endpoint","Create a SageMaker Model Monitor schedule","Review detected data quality violations in Amazon CloudWatch"]'::json,
  '{1,0,2,3}'::int[],
  'Setting up SageMaker Model Monitor for data quality involves a specific sequence. Option B (Configure data capture on the SageMaker endpoint) is the essential first step to collect inference request and response data. Once data is being captured, Option A (Generate a baseline for model data) establishes the expected data distribution. With a baseline in place, Option C (Create a SageMaker Model Monitor schedule) defines when and how often the monitor will run. Finally, Option D (Review detected data quality violations in Amazon CloudWatch) is the ongoing step to analyze the monitoring results.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain17_3',
  NOW(),
  9,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_17_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_17_m_17_2_132',
  'A financial services company relies on an Amazon SageMaker model for credit risk assessment. The model''s performance can degrade due to evolving economic conditions, necessitating retraining. To maintain high accuracy and minimize operational overhead, they want to implement a retraining strategy that is triggered automatically when significant data drift is detected, rather than relying solely on fixed schedules. Order the following steps to implement a drift-triggered retraining mechanism.',
  'ordering',
  '["Configure a SageMaker Model Monitor schedule to continuously analyze inference data for drift and send metrics to Amazon CloudWatch.","Set up an Amazon CloudWatch Alarm that triggers when Model Monitor detects data drift exceeding a predefined threshold.","Develop an AWS Lambda function to initiate a new SageMaker training job using the latest data, triggered by the CloudWatch Alarm.","Establish a baseline for data quality using SageMaker Model Monitor on a representative dataset."]'::json,
  '{3,0,1,2}'::int[],
  'Option D (Establish a baseline for data quality...) is the essential first step, as it defines the ''normal'' data distribution against which drift will be measured. Option A (Configure a SageMaker Model Monitor schedule...) then sets up the continuous monitoring of production data for deviations. Option B (Set up an Amazon CloudWatch Alarm...) is configured to detect significant drift based on Model Monitor''s output. Finally, Option C (Develop an AWS Lambda function to initiate a new SageMaker training job...) is the automated response, triggering retraining when the alarm state is reached. This sequence implements a responsive, drift-triggered retraining strategy.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain17_3',
  NOW(),
  10,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_17_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_17_m_17_2_133',
  'A pharmaceutical research firm uses Amazon SageMaker for developing new drug discovery models. For regulatory compliance and scientific reproducibility, they need to meticulously track the lineage of all model artifacts, input datasets, and training job configurations. This ensures transparency and auditability of the entire ML development process. Order the following steps to effectively utilize Amazon SageMaker ML Lineage Tracking for a training job.',
  'ordering',
  '["Define the input datasets (e.g., S3 URIs) and output model artifacts for the SageMaker training job.","Execute the SageMaker training job, which automatically records its associated components and relationships in ML Lineage Tracking.","Use the SageMaker Python SDK to retrieve and visualize the lineage graph for the completed training job.","Ensure the IAM role used by the SageMaker training job has permissions to write lineage data."]'::json,
  '{0,3,1,2}'::int[],
  'Option A (Define the input datasets...) is the logical starting point, as these are the primary entities whose lineage needs to be tracked. Option D (Ensure the IAM role used by the SageMaker training job...) is a prerequisite to allow SageMaker to record lineage information. Option B (Execute the SageMaker training job...) is when the lineage data is automatically captured by SageMaker. Finally, Option C (Use the SageMaker Python SDK to retrieve and visualize...) allows the team to inspect and audit the recorded lineage. This sequence ensures that the lineage of the training process is properly captured and accessible.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain17_3',
  NOW(),
  11,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_17_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_17_m_17_2_134',
  'A data science team manages an Amazon SageMaker model for predicting customer churn. The model''s performance tends to degrade gradually over several months due to evolving customer behavior patterns. To proactively maintain model accuracy and avoid significant performance drops, the team decides to implement a scheduled retraining strategy. Order the following steps to set up automated scheduled retraining for the SageMaker model.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create an AWS Lambda function to trigger a SageMaker training job using the latest dataset.","Define the SageMaker training job configuration, including the algorithm, instance types, and S3 paths for data and output.","Set up an Amazon EventBridge rule to invoke the Lambda function on a predefined schedule (e.g., monthly).","Prepare and store the latest training dataset in an Amazon S3 bucket, ensuring it''s accessible by SageMaker."]'::json,
  '{3,1,0,2}'::int[],
  'Option D (Prepare and store the latest training dataset...) is the prerequisite, as the retraining job needs access to fresh data. Option B (Define the SageMaker training job configuration...) specifies how the model will be retrained. Option A (Create an AWS Lambda function to trigger a SageMaker training job...) provides the programmatic interface to start the training process. Finally, Option C (Set up an Amazon EventBridge rule to invoke the Lambda function...) automates the execution of the Lambda function, thereby triggering the retraining job at regular intervals. This sequence establishes a robust scheduled retraining pipeline.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain17_3',
  NOW(),
  12,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_17_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_17_m_17_2_135',
  'A startup has deployed an Amazon SageMaker real-time inference endpoint for their new mobile application. The traffic to this endpoint is highly variable, with peak usage during specific hours and low usage overnight. To optimize costs while maintaining responsiveness, they need to configure the endpoint to automatically scale its instances based on demand. Order the following steps to implement auto-scaling for a SageMaker inference endpoint.',
  'ordering',
  '["Register the SageMaker endpoint variant as a scalable target with Application Auto Scaling.","Create an Amazon SageMaker endpoint configuration and deploy the endpoint with a single variant.","Define scaling policies (e.g., target tracking) for the scalable target based on metrics like `InvocationsPerInstance`.","Enable auto-scaling for the SageMaker endpoint by specifying minimum and maximum instance counts for the variant."]'::json,
  '{1,3,0,2}'::int[],
  'Option B (Create an Amazon SageMaker endpoint configuration and deploy the endpoint...) is the initial step to get the endpoint running. Option D (Enable auto-scaling for the SageMaker endpoint by specifying minimum and maximum instance counts...) configures the basic auto-scaling parameters for the endpoint variant. Option A (Register the SageMaker endpoint variant as a scalable target...) makes the endpoint variant manageable by Application Auto Scaling. Finally, Option C (Define scaling policies... based on metrics like `InvocationsPerInstance`.) sets the specific rules that govern when and how the endpoint scales up or down. This sequence ensures the endpoint can dynamically adjust to varying traffic, optimizing cost and performance.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain17_3',
  NOW(),
  13,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_17_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_17_m_17_2_136',
  'A data analytics firm needs to ensure full traceability of their ML models, from the raw data sources in Amazon S3 through various preprocessing steps, to the final training job in Amazon SageMaker. This is crucial for debugging, auditing, and understanding the impact of data changes on model performance. Order the following steps to track data and model lineage using Amazon SageMaker ML Lineage Tracking.',
  'ordering',
  '["Define the input datasets (e.g., S3 URIs) and output model artifacts for the SageMaker training job.","Execute the SageMaker training job, allowing ML Lineage Tracking to automatically capture associations between inputs, job, and outputs.","Use the SageMaker Python SDK to query and visualize the lineage graph, showing the flow from data to model.","Ensure the IAM role used by the SageMaker training job has the necessary permissions to interact with ML Lineage Tracking."]'::json,
  '{0,3,1,2}'::int[],
  'Option A (Define the input datasets...) is the starting point, as these are the primary entities whose lineage needs to be tracked. Option D (Ensure the IAM role used by the SageMaker training job...) is a prerequisite to allow SageMaker to record lineage information. Option B (Execute the SageMaker training job...) is when the lineage data is automatically captured by SageMaker. Finally, Option C (Use the SageMaker Python SDK to query and visualize...) allows the team to inspect and audit the recorded lineage, providing a clear view of data provenance. This sequence ensures comprehensive lineage tracking.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain17_3',
  NOW(),
  14,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_17_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_17_m_17_2_137',
  'A machine learning team needs to optimize the cost of their Amazon SageMaker inference endpoint. Arrange the following steps in the correct order to achieve cost efficiency.',
  'ordering',
  '["Analyze current endpoint usage and metrics using Amazon CloudWatch.","Configure SageMaker auto-scaling policies based on utilization.","Evaluate and apply right-sizing recommendations for instance types.","Identify underutilized instances or opportunities for auto-scaling."]'::json,
  '{0,3,1,2}'::int[],
  'To optimize SageMaker inference endpoint costs, the first step is to analyze current usage and metrics (Option A) to understand the baseline. Next, identify underutilized instances or opportunities for auto-scaling (Option D) based on the analysis. Then, configure SageMaker auto-scaling policies (Option B) to dynamically adjust capacity. Finally, evaluate and apply right-sizing recommendations for instance types (Option C) to ensure the most cost-effective instances are used.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain17_3',
  NOW(),
  15,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_17_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_17_m_17_2_138',
  'A data scientist wants to set up basic monitoring for a newly deployed Amazon SageMaker inference endpoint. Arrange the following steps in the correct order to view standard endpoint metrics in Amazon CloudWatch.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create a custom dashboard to visualize endpoint latency and throughput.","Access Amazon CloudWatch console.","Deploy the SageMaker inference endpoint.","Navigate to SageMaker metrics under \"All metrics\" in CloudWatch."]'::json,
  '{2,1,3,0}'::int[],
  'The first step to monitor a SageMaker endpoint is to deploy the endpoint itself (Option C), as metrics are only generated after deployment. Next, access the Amazon CloudWatch console (Option B). From there, navigate to the SageMaker metrics (Option D) to view default metrics like latency and throughput. Finally, you can create a custom dashboard (Option A) to visualize these metrics effectively.',
