  'quiz_domain17_3',
  NOW(),
  17,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_17_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_17_m_17_2_140',
  'Order the types of metrics Amazon CloudWatch provides for SageMaker endpoints.',
  'ordering',
  '["Error rates (e.g., 4xx, 5xx errors)","Latency (e.g., ModelLatency, OverheadLatency)","Throughput (e.g., Invocations, InvocationsPerInstance)","Resource utilization (e.g., CPUUtilization, MemoryUtilization)"]'::json,
  '{1,2,0,3}'::int[],
  'Amazon CloudWatch provides several key metrics for SageMaker endpoints. These include Latency metrics (Option B) such as ModelLatency and OverheadLatency, which measure the time taken for inference. Throughput metrics (Option C) like Invocations and InvocationsPerInstance track the volume of requests. Error rates (Option A) monitor the number of 4xx or 5xx errors encountered. Lastly, Resource utilization metrics (Option D) such as CPUUtilization and MemoryUtilization provide insights into the underlying instance performance.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain17_3',
  NOW(),
  18,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_17_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_17_m_17_2_141',
  'An ML team wants to optimize the cost of SageMaker training jobs by leveraging Spot Instances. Order the steps to configure a training job to use Spot Instances.',
  'ordering',
  '["Specify the maximum wait time for a Spot Instance to become available.","Set the `use_spot_instances` parameter to `True` in the SageMaker Estimator.","Define the maximum run time for the training job.","Configure checkpointing for the training job to save progress."]'::json,
  '{1,0,2,3}'::int[],
  'To configure a SageMaker training job to use Spot Instances, the first step is to set the `use_spot_instances` parameter to `True` within the SageMaker Estimator configuration (Option B). Next, specify the `max_wait_time` parameter, which defines how long SageMaker should wait for a Spot Instance to become available before failing the job (Option A). It''s also crucial to define the `max_run_time` for the training job, as Spot Instances can be interrupted (Option C). Finally, configure checkpointing for the training job to periodically save its progress, allowing it to resume from the last checkpoint if interrupted (Option D).',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain17_3',
  NOW(),
  19,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_17_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_17_m_17_2_142',
  'Order the actions typically taken when a CloudWatch alarm for a SageMaker endpoint metric is triggered, indicating a performance issue.',
  'ordering',
  '["Investigate the root cause of the performance issue using CloudWatch Logs and metrics.","Receive a notification via Amazon SNS that the alarm has triggered.","Evaluate the impact of the issue on model performance or user experience.","Implement a remediation action, such as scaling up or retraining the model."]'::json,
  '{1,2,0,3}'::int[],
  'When a CloudWatch alarm for a SageMaker endpoint metric is triggered, the first action is to receive a notification, typically via an Amazon SNS topic (Option B). Upon notification, it''s important to evaluate the immediate impact of the performance issue on the model''s effectiveness or the end-user experience (Option C). Subsequently, a thorough investigation of the root cause is performed using detailed CloudWatch Logs and other relevant metrics (Option A). Finally, based on the investigation, a remediation action is implemented, which could involve scaling up the endpoint, retraining the model, or adjusting traffic routing (Option D).',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain17_3',
  NOW(),
  20,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_17_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_17_m_17_2_143',
  'A data science team needs to regularly retrain a model when significant data drift is detected. Order the steps to automate this retraining trigger using SageMaker Model Monitor and CloudWatch Alarms.',
  'ordering',
  '["Configure a CloudWatch Event Rule to trigger an AWS Lambda function on the alarm state change.","Set up SageMaker Model Monitor to detect data drift and generate violations.","Create a CloudWatch Alarm that triggers when Model Monitor detects a drift violation.","Develop an AWS Lambda function to initiate a SageMaker training job."]'::json,
  '{1,2,3,0}'::int[],
  'To automate retraining on data drift, the first step is to set up SageMaker Model Monitor to continuously analyze data quality and detect drift violations (Option B). When Model Monitor detects a violation, a CloudWatch Alarm is created to trigger based on these violations (Option C). Next, an AWS Lambda function is developed to encapsulate the logic for initiating a SageMaker training job (Option D). Finally, a CloudWatch Event Rule is configured to invoke this Lambda function whenever the CloudWatch Alarm transitions to an ''ALARM'' state, thus automating the retraining process (Option A).',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain17_3',
  NOW(),
  21,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_17_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_17_m_17_2_144',
  'Order the general process for right-sizing SageMaker instances for cost optimization.',
  'ordering',
