  '{0,1,3,2}'::int[],
  'The process of right-sizing begins by monitoring the resource utilization (CPU, memory, GPU) of the currently used SageMaker instance (Option A). Next, historical usage patterns are analyzed to understand typical and peak loads (Option B). Based on this data, different instance types are benchmarked with representative workloads to find the most efficient option (Option D). Finally, the instance type or count is adjusted based on the analysis, and the new configuration is continuously re-evaluated for optimal performance and cost (Option C).',
