  'To detect drift in feature attribution, you first need a reference. Option A (Generate a baseline for feature attribution) provides this initial benchmark. Next, you define the input for the monitoring job, so Option B (Configure a `ModelBiasJobInput` in the monitoring schedule) specifies the data to be analyzed for bias. With the baseline and input ready, Option C (Create a SageMaker Model Monitor schedule) sets up the recurring monitoring. Finally, Option D (Review the bias reports for feature attribution drift) allows you to inspect the results for any significant changes.',
