INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_17_m_17_1_130',
  'A large e-commerce company deploys a personalized recommendation model on an Amazon SageMaker real-time endpoint. To ensure the model continues to provide relevant recommendations and to detect any degradation in its predictive quality, the MLOps team needs to implement continuous monitoring. They aim to capture inference data, establish a performance baseline, and receive automated alerts if the model''s quality deviates significantly. Order the following steps to correctly set up Amazon SageMaker Model Monitor for model quality monitoring and integrate it with Amazon CloudWatch for alerts.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create a SageMaker Model Monitor schedule to continuously analyze captured inference data against the established baseline.","Configure the SageMaker endpoint to enable data capture, storing inference requests and responses in a specified Amazon S3 bucket.","Set up Amazon CloudWatch Alarms based on the model quality metrics generated by SageMaker Model Monitor to trigger notifications.","Run a SageMaker Model Monitor baseline job on a representative dataset to generate baseline statistics and constraints for model quality."]'::json,
  '{3,1,0,2}'::int[],
  'Option D (Run a SageMaker Model Monitor baseline job...) is the foundational step, as a baseline of expected model quality is essential for comparison. Option B (Configure the SageMaker endpoint to enable data capture...) must follow to collect the actual inference data that will be monitored. Option A (Create a SageMaker Model Monitor schedule...) then initiates the continuous analysis of this captured data against the baseline. Finally, Option C (Set up Amazon CloudWatch Alarms...) integrates the monitoring with an alerting system, ensuring the team is proactively notified of any detected model quality drift. This sequence establishes a comprehensive and automated model quality monitoring system.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain17_3',
  NOW(),
  30,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_17_1',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_17_m_17_1_131',
  'A financial institution uses an Amazon SageMaker endpoint for real-time fraud detection. Due to evolving fraud patterns, the model''s data distribution can shift, leading to data drift and potential accuracy degradation. The MLOps team needs to establish a robust monitoring system to detect data quality issues and bias drift, ensuring the model remains fair and effective. Order the following steps to implement continuous data quality and bias drift monitoring using Amazon SageMaker Model Monitor.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create a SageMaker Model Monitor schedule to continuously analyze the captured data for data quality and bias drift.","Configure the SageMaker endpoint to capture inference requests and responses, storing them in an Amazon S3 bucket.","Define and run a SageMaker Model Monitor baseline job on a representative dataset, including configuration for data quality and bias metrics.","Set up Amazon CloudWatch Alarms to alert the team when data quality or bias drift is detected by Model Monitor."]'::json,
  '{2,1,0,3}'::int[],
  'Option C (Define and run a SageMaker Model Monitor baseline job...) is the crucial first step, as it establishes the reference point for data quality and bias metrics against which future inference data will be compared. Option B (Configure the SageMaker endpoint to capture inference requests and responses...) must be performed next to collect the actual data from the production endpoint. Option A (Create a SageMaker Model Monitor schedule...) then sets up the automated process to analyze this captured data for drift. Finally, Option D (Set up Amazon CloudWatch Alarms...) ensures that the team is promptly notified when drift is detected, enabling a timely response. This comprehensive setup addresses both data quality and bias drift concerns.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain17_3',
  NOW(),
  31,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_17_1',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_17_m_17_1_132',
  'A media company uses an Amazon SageMaker endpoint for content recommendation, and they need to track its operational performance metrics like invocation latency and throughput to ensure a smooth user experience. The operations team wants to visualize these metrics and receive immediate alerts if performance degrades below acceptable thresholds. Order the following steps to set up comprehensive monitoring for a SageMaker endpoint''s operational health using Amazon CloudWatch.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create Amazon CloudWatch Alarms based on the SageMaker endpoint metrics (e.g., `Invocations`, `InvocationLatency`) to notify on threshold breaches.","Access the Amazon CloudWatch console to view the default metrics automatically emitted by the SageMaker endpoint.","Create a custom Amazon CloudWatch Dashboard to visualize key SageMaker endpoint performance metrics over time.","Identify the specific SageMaker endpoint and its associated metrics within the CloudWatch console."]'::json,
  '{1,3,2,0}'::int[],
  'Option B (Access the Amazon CloudWatch console...) is the initial step to begin monitoring, as CloudWatch automatically collects metrics for SageMaker endpoints. Option D (Identify the specific SageMaker endpoint and its associated metrics...) is necessary to locate and focus on the relevant data. Option C (Create a custom Amazon CloudWatch Dashboard...) allows for organized visualization of these metrics, providing a holistic view of performance. Finally, Option A (Create Amazon CloudWatch Alarms...) ensures that the team receives proactive alerts for any critical performance issues, enabling rapid response. This sequence ensures both visibility and proactive alerting for operational health.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain17_3',
  NOW(),
  32,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_17_1',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_17_m_17_1_133',
  'A healthcare organization has deployed an ML model on Amazon SageMaker for predicting patient outcomes. They are concerned about concept drift, where the underlying relationship between input features and target variables changes over time, potentially leading to inaccurate predictions. The team needs to detect this drift and respond effectively. Order the following steps to implement a strategy for detecting and responding to concept drift using SageMaker Model Monitor and CloudWatch.',
  'ordering',
  '["Analyze the detected drift using SageMaker Model Monitor reports to understand the nature and impact of the concept drift.","Configure the SageMaker endpoint for data capture to an Amazon S3 bucket to collect inference data.","Set up Amazon CloudWatch Alarms to trigger when SageMaker Model Monitor detects significant model quality drift.","Establish a baseline for model quality metrics using SageMaker Model Monitor on a representative dataset."]'::json,
  '{3,1,2,0}'::int[],
  'Option D (Establish a baseline for model quality metrics...) is the fundamental first step, providing a reference point for expected model performance. Option B (Configure the SageMaker endpoint for data capture...) is necessary to collect the actual production inference data for monitoring. Option C (Set up Amazon CloudWatch Alarms to trigger when SageMaker Model Monitor detects significant model quality drift...) ensures that the team is alerted when concept drift, manifested as model quality degradation, occurs. Finally, Option A (Analyze the detected drift using SageMaker Model Monitor reports...) allows for a detailed investigation into the root cause and severity of the drift, informing subsequent maintenance actions. This process enables proactive detection and informed response to concept drift.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain17_3',
  NOW(),
  33,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_17_1',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_17_m_17_1_134',
  'A logistics company uses an Amazon SageMaker endpoint for optimizing delivery routes. They need to ensure high availability and responsiveness of the endpoint while also monitoring for any performance bottlenecks or errors. The MLOps team wants to track key operational metrics and be alerted immediately if the endpoint experiences a high error rate or increased latency. Order the following steps to establish robust operational monitoring for the SageMaker endpoint.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create Amazon CloudWatch Alarms on the `InvocationError` and `InvocationLatency` metrics to alert on critical thresholds.","Navigate to the Amazon CloudWatch console and select the ''Metrics'' section to browse available SageMaker endpoint metrics.","Identify the specific SageMaker endpoint''s namespace and dimensions (e.g., `EndpointName`) to filter relevant metrics.","Develop a custom Amazon CloudWatch Dashboard to visualize the endpoint''s `Invocations`, `InvocationLatency`, and `InvocationError` metrics."]'::json,
  '{1,2,3,0}'::int[],
  'Option B (Navigate to the Amazon CloudWatch console...) is the starting point for accessing monitoring data. Option C (Identify the specific SageMaker endpoint''s namespace and dimensions...) is crucial to narrow down and select the correct metrics for the target endpoint. Option D (Develop a custom Amazon CloudWatch Dashboard...) provides a centralized and visual representation of the endpoint''s performance, making it easier to observe trends. Finally, Option A (Create Amazon CloudWatch Alarms...) is essential for proactive incident management, ensuring that the team is notified immediately of any performance degradation or errors. This sequence ensures comprehensive operational monitoring and alerting.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain17_3',
  NOW(),
  34,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_17_1',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_17_m_17_1_135',
  'A pharmaceutical company uses an Amazon SageMaker model for predicting drug efficacy. To maintain trust and explainability, they need to monitor for feature attribution drift, ensuring that the importance of input features remains consistent over time. Any significant change could indicate data shifts or model issues that affect interpretability. Order the following steps to set up feature attribution drift monitoring using Amazon SageMaker Model Monitor.',
  'ordering',
  '["Configure the SageMaker endpoint to capture inference requests and responses, including feature attributions, to an Amazon S3 bucket.","Set up Amazon CloudWatch Alarms based on the feature attribution drift metrics generated by SageMaker Model Monitor.","Define and run a SageMaker Model Monitor baseline job, specifying the feature attribution method and target features.","Create a SageMaker Model Monitor schedule to continuously analyze the captured data for feature attribution drift."]'::json,
  '{2,0,3,1}'::int[],
  'Option C (Define and run a SageMaker Model Monitor baseline job...) is the initial step, as it establishes the expected feature attribution patterns against which future inferences will be compared. Option A (Configure the SageMaker endpoint to capture inference requests and responses...) is necessary to collect the real-time data, including feature attributions, from the production endpoint. Option D (Create a SageMaker Model Monitor schedule...) then automates the continuous analysis of this captured data for any deviations in feature attributions. Finally, Option B (Set up Amazon CloudWatch Alarms...) ensures that the team is alerted to significant drift, allowing for timely investigation and remediation to maintain model explainability. This sequence ensures robust monitoring of feature attribution drift.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain17_3',
  NOW(),
  35,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_17_1',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_17_m_17_1_136',
  'A manufacturing company uses an ML model deployed on Amazon SageMaker for predictive maintenance. They want to ensure the model''s predictions remain accurate and reliable over time, as data characteristics can subtly change due to sensor degradation or process variations. The MLOps team needs to establish a system to detect data drift and model quality degradation, triggering automated alerts. Order the following steps to implement a comprehensive monitoring solution.',
  'ordering',
  '["Configure the SageMaker endpoint to enable data capture, storing inference requests and responses in an Amazon S3 bucket.","Create a SageMaker Model Monitor schedule to continuously analyze the captured data against the established baseline for data and model quality.","Set up Amazon CloudWatch Alarms based on the drift metrics from SageMaker Model Monitor to send notifications.","Run a SageMaker Model Monitor baseline job on a representative dataset to generate baseline statistics and constraints for data and model quality."]'::json,
  '{3,0,1,2}'::int[],
  'Option D (Run a SageMaker Model Monitor baseline job...) is the essential first step, as it establishes the ''normal'' behavior for data and model quality against which future data will be compared. Option A (Configure the SageMaker endpoint to enable data capture...) is then necessary to collect the actual inference data from the production environment. Option B (Create a SageMaker Model Monitor schedule...) automates the process of comparing this captured data to the baseline. Finally, Option C (Set up Amazon CloudWatch Alarms...) ensures that the team is alerted to any detected drift, enabling prompt investigation and action. This sequence creates an effective, automated monitoring system.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain17_3',
  NOW(),
  36,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_17_1',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_17_m_17_1_137',
  'A retail company has deployed an Amazon SageMaker model for demand forecasting. The underlying market conditions and customer behaviors are dynamic, leading to potential data drift that can degrade model accuracy. The MLOps team needs to establish a system to detect this drift and receive automated alerts, focusing on the input features. Order the following steps to set up data quality drift monitoring for the SageMaker endpoint''s input features.',
  'ordering',
  '["Configure the SageMaker endpoint to enable data capture, storing input features from inference requests in an Amazon S3 bucket.","Create a SageMaker Model Monitor schedule to continuously analyze the captured input features against the established baseline.","Set up Amazon CloudWatch Alarms based on the data quality drift metrics generated by SageMaker Model Monitor to trigger alerts.","Run a SageMaker Model Monitor baseline job on a representative dataset of input features to generate baseline statistics and constraints."]'::json,
  '{3,0,1,2}'::int[],
  'Option D (Run a SageMaker Model Monitor baseline job...) is the critical first step, as it defines the expected distribution and characteristics of the input features. Option A (Configure the SageMaker endpoint to enable data capture...) is then required to collect the actual input features being sent to the production endpoint. Option B (Create a SageMaker Model Monitor schedule...) automates the comparison of these captured features against the baseline. Finally, Option C (Set up Amazon CloudWatch Alarms...) ensures that the team receives timely notifications when significant data quality drift is detected, allowing for proactive model maintenance. This sequence establishes a robust data quality monitoring system.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain17_3',
  NOW(),
  37,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_17_1',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_17_m_17_1_138',
  'Order the typical sequence for detecting and responding to model drift in a SageMaker production environment.',
  'ordering',
  '["Analyze monitoring reports to understand the nature of the drift.","Deploy the new model version to the SageMaker endpoint.","Set up SageMaker Model Monitor to detect data or model quality drift.","Retrain the model with updated data or a new algorithm."]'::json,
  '{2,0,3,1}'::int[],
  'The process begins by setting up SageMaker Model Monitor to continuously detect data or model quality drift (Option C). Once drift is detected and alerts are triggered, the next step is to analyze the monitoring reports to understand the root cause and characteristics of the drift (Option A). Based on this analysis, the model is then retrained with updated data or potentially a new algorithm to address the drift (Option D). Finally, the newly retrained and validated model version is deployed to the SageMaker endpoint to replace the drifting model (Option B).',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain17_3',
  NOW(),
  38,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_17_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_17_m_17_1_139',
  'A data scientist wants to set up automated alerts for high inference latency on a SageMaker endpoint. Order the steps to achieve this using Amazon CloudWatch.',
  'ordering',
  '["Create an Amazon CloudWatch alarm based on the chosen metric and threshold.","Identify the relevant latency metric for the SageMaker endpoint in CloudWatch.","Configure an Amazon SNS topic for notifications.","Associate the SNS topic with the CloudWatch alarm."]'::json,
  '{1,0,2,3}'::int[],
  'The first step is to identify the specific latency metric emitted by the SageMaker endpoint that needs to be monitored within Amazon CloudWatch (Option B). Once the metric is identified, an Amazon CloudWatch alarm is created, specifying the threshold at which an alert should be triggered (Option A). To receive notifications when the alarm state changes, an Amazon SNS topic must be configured (Option C). Finally, this SNS topic is associated with the CloudWatch alarm as an action to send notifications (Option D).',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain17_3',
  NOW(),
  39,
  NULL,
  NULL,
  'm_17_1',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
