  'The initial step for any IAM role is its creation. Option C (Create a new IAM role in the AWS Management Console) starts the process. Next, you define who can use the role, so Option B (Define a trust policy allowing `sagemaker.amazonaws.com` to assume the role) is essential for SageMaker to use it. Then, you grant permissions to the role, making Option A (Attach the `AmazonSageMakerFullAccess` managed policy) the next logical step. Finally, Option D (Review and create the IAM role) completes the role creation.',
