  'Match the feature selection and dimensionality reduction technique to its goal.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"Principal Component Analysis (PCA)","B":"Correlation analysis","C":"Feature importance"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'Principal Component Analysis (PCA) (Option A) is a dimensionality reduction technique that transforms a set of possibly correlated features into a smaller set of uncorrelated features (principal components) while retaining most of the variance. Correlation analysis (Option B) is used to identify linear relationships between features, helping to detect multicollinearity or strong predictors. Feature importance (Option C) methods, often derived from tree-based models, rank features by their contribution to model predictions, aiding in selecting the most relevant features.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain14_3',
  NOW(),
  31,
  '{"left":["Principal Component Analysis (PCA)","Correlation analysis","Feature importance"],"right":["Reduces feature count while retaining variance","Identifies linear relationships between features","Ranks features by their impact on model predictions"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2],"right":[0,1,2]}'::jsonb,
  'm_14_2',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

