  NULL,
  'Random split (Option A) is a general-purpose method that divides data without specific order, suitable for independent and identically distributed data. Stratified split (Option B) is crucial when dealing with imbalanced datasets, as it ensures that the proportion of target classes is maintained in each subset. Time-series split (Option C) is essential for time-dependent data to prevent data leakage from future observations into the training set, which would lead to an overly optimistic model evaluation (anti-pattern: ap-1.3-001).',
