  NULL,
  'The correct pairings are: ''Random split for time-series'' with ''Use time-based split'', ''Fitting scaler on test data'' with ''Fit scaler on training data'', and ''No bias detection'' with ''Use SageMaker Clarify''. Using a random split for time-series data can lead to data leakage, so a time-based split is essential. Fitting data transformers like scalers on test data (or the entire dataset before splitting) causes data leakage; they should only be fit on training data. Not detecting bias can lead to unfair models, which Amazon SageMaker Clarify helps address.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain14_3',
  NOW(),
  59,
  '{"left":["Random split for time-series","Fitting scaler on test data","No bias detection"],"right":["Fit scaler on training data","Use SageMaker Clarify","Use time-based split"]}'::json,
