  'Data parallelism (Option A) involves distributing different mini-batches of data to multiple training instances, with each instance training a replica of the model. Model parallelism (Option B) is used when a model is too large to fit on a single GPU; it involves distributing different layers or parts of the model across multiple instances or GPUs.',
