INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_2_162',
  'An MLOps team is establishing a robust continuous integration and continuous delivery (CI/CD) pipeline for machine learning models on AWS. They need to integrate various tools to automate the build, test, and deployment phases, ensuring version control, artifact management, and workflow orchestration. The architect must precisely identify the role of each core service within this integrated MLOps framework to design an efficient and maintainable system.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"AWS CodePipeline","B":"AWS CodeBuild","C":"Amazon ECR","D":"SageMaker Model Registry"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'AWS CodePipeline (Option A) is designed to orchestrate the entire software release process, making it central to an MLOps CI/CD pipeline. AWS CodeBuild (Option B) is used for compiling code, running tests, and generating artifacts, which is crucial for building model containers. Amazon ECR (Option C) provides a managed Docker container registry, essential for storing and managing the container images of ML models. SageMaker Model Registry (Option D) offers a centralized repository for model versions, enabling governance, lineage tracking, and approval workflows before deployment.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  17,
  '{"left":["AWS CodePipeline","AWS CodeBuild","Amazon ECR","SageMaker Model Registry"],"right":["Orchestrates the entire software release process, including ML model deployment stages.","Compiles source code, runs tests, and produces deployable artifacts like Docker images.","Stores, manages, and deploys Docker container images for ML models.","Manages model versions, lineage, and approval workflows for deployment."]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2,3],"right":[0,1,2,3]}'::jsonb,
  'm_16_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_2_163',
  'A data science team is adopting Infrastructure as Code (IaC) principles to manage their Amazon SageMaker resources, aiming for reproducibility, version control, and automated provisioning. They are evaluating different AWS services and tools to define and deploy their ML infrastructure. Understanding the distinct capabilities of each tool is critical for selecting the appropriate approach for various components of their ML workflow.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"AWS CloudFormation","B":"AWS Cloud Development Kit (CDK)","C":"Docker","D":"SageMaker Pipelines"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'AWS CloudFormation (Option A) is a declarative service for defining AWS infrastructure using templates, enabling consistent and repeatable deployments. AWS CDK (Option B) provides a programmatic way to define cloud resources using high-level programming languages, offering more abstraction and reusability. Docker (Option C) is a standard for containerization, crucial for packaging ML models and their dependencies. SageMaker Pipelines (Option D) is specifically designed to orchestrate entire ML workflows, which can include provisioning SageMaker-specific infrastructure as part of its steps.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  18,
  '{"left":["AWS CloudFormation","AWS Cloud Development Kit (CDK)","Docker","SageMaker Pipelines"],"right":["Declarative language for defining AWS resources using templates (YAML/JSON).","Programmatic approach to define cloud infrastructure using familiar programming languages.","Platform for developing, shipping, and running applications in containers.","Orchestrates end-to-end machine learning workflows, including infrastructure provisioning."]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2,3],"right":[0,1,2,3]}'::jsonb,
  'm_16_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_2_164',
  'A pharmaceutical company is developing a new drug discovery platform that leverages machine learning. They need to containerize their complex ML models, including custom libraries and specific runtime environments, to ensure consistency across development, testing, and production. The architect must select the appropriate AWS services for building, storing, and deploying these containerized models.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"Docker","B":"Amazon ECR","C":"AWS CodeBuild","D":"SageMaker Hosting"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'Docker (Option A) is the foundational technology for containerization, allowing models and their environments to be packaged. Amazon ECR (Option B) is the managed AWS service for storing and managing these Docker container images. AWS CodeBuild (Option C) can be used within a CI/CD pipeline to build the Docker images for the ML models. SageMaker Hosting (Option D) is the service that deploys these containerized models as scalable inference endpoints.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  19,
  '{"left":["Docker","Amazon ECR","AWS CodeBuild","SageMaker Hosting"],"right":["Technology for packaging applications and dependencies into portable containers.","Fully managed Docker container registry for storing and sharing container images.","Service for compiling source code, running tests, and producing Docker images.","Managed service for deploying and managing ML models as inference endpoints."]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2,3],"right":[0,1,2,3]}'::jsonb,
  'm_16_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_16_m_16_2_165',
  'A research institution is developing a complex machine learning model that requires significant computational resources for training and inference. They need to provision and manage the underlying infrastructure for their SageMaker experiments and deployments using Infrastructure as Code (IaC) to ensure reproducibility and version control. The MLOps engineer must select the appropriate tools for defining and deploying these resources.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"AWS CloudFormation","B":"AWS Cloud Development Kit (CDK)","C":"Amazon ECR","D":"SageMaker Studio"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'AWS CloudFormation (Option A) is a declarative IaC service that allows defining AWS resources using templates, ensuring consistent provisioning. AWS CDK (Option B) provides a programmatic approach to IaC, enabling developers to define cloud infrastructure using high-level programming languages. Amazon ECR (Option C) is a managed container registry, essential for storing Docker images of custom ML models. SageMaker Studio (Option D) is an IDE for ML development, not an IaC tool, though it integrates with resources provisioned by IaC.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain16_3',
  NOW(),
  20,
  '{"left":["AWS CloudFormation","AWS Cloud Development Kit (CDK)","Amazon ECR","SageMaker Studio"],"right":["Declarative service for modeling and provisioning AWS resources through templates.","Framework for defining cloud infrastructure using familiar programming languages.","Managed Docker container registry for storing and managing model images.","Integrated development environment (IDE) for machine learning on SageMaker."]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2,3],"right":[0,1,2,3]}'::jsonb,
  'm_16_2',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

