  NULL,
  'The Least Privilege Principle (Option A) dictates that users and services should only be granted the minimum permissions required to perform their tasks. Resource-based Policies (Option B) are attached directly to an AWS resource, such as an Amazon S3 bucket, to specify who has access to that resource and what actions they can perform. Identity-based Policies (Option C) are attached to an IAM user, group, or role to control what actions that identity can perform.',
