  '{"A":"AWS IAM","B":"AWS KMS","C":"Amazon VPC"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'AWS IAM (left item 0) provides ''Access control'' (right item 0) for AWS resources, allowing you to manage who can access your ML workloads and what actions they can perform. AWS KMS (left item 1) is used for ''Encryption key management'' (right item 1), enabling you to create and control the encryption keys used to encrypt your data. Amazon VPC (left item 2) allows you to provision a logically isolated section of the AWS Cloud, providing ''Network isolation'' (right item 2) for your SageMaker training jobs and endpoints.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain17_3',
  NOW(),
  45,
  '{"left":["AWS IAM","AWS KMS","Amazon VPC"],"right":["Access control","Encryption key management","Network isolation"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2],"right":[0,1,2]}'::jsonb,
  'm_17_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_17_m_17_3_118',
  'A company requires secure SageMaker training jobs in a regulated environment. Match the security control to its purpose.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"Data access permissions","B":"Network isolation","C":"Credential management"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'For ''Data access permissions'' (left item 0) to resources like Amazon S3 buckets, AWS IAM roles (right item 0) are used to grant SageMaker training jobs the necessary permissions. ''Network isolation'' (left item 1) for training jobs, preventing direct internet access and ensuring private communication, is achieved through Amazon VPC configuration (right item 1). ''Credential management'' (left item 2) for sensitive information like API keys or database passwords is best handled by AWS Secrets Manager (right item 2), which securely stores and retrieves secrets.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain17_3',
  NOW(),
  46,
  '{"left":["Data access permissions","Network isolation","Credential management"],"right":["AWS IAM roles","Amazon VPC configuration","AWS Secrets Manager"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2],"right":[0,1,2]}'::jsonb,
  'm_17_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_17_m_17_3_119',
  'Match the data state to the type of encryption typically applied in AWS.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"Data at rest","B":"Data in transit"}'::json,
  NULL,
  '''Data at rest'' (left item 0), referring to data stored in services like Amazon S3 or Amazon EBS, is typically protected using ''Server-side encryption'' (right item 0) with AWS KMS or S3-managed keys. ''Data in transit'' (left item 1), referring to data moving between services or over networks, is secured using ''TLS/SSL encryption'' (right item 1) to protect against eavesdropping and tampering.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain17_3',
  NOW(),
  47,
  '{"left":["Data at rest","Data in transit"],"right":["Server-side encryption","TLS/SSL encryption"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1],"right":[0,1]}'::jsonb,
  'm_17_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_17_m_17_3_120',
  'Match AWS IAM components to their function in SageMaker environments.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"IAM roles","B":"IAM policies","C":"SageMaker execution role"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'IAM roles (left item 0) are used to ''Delegate permissions to services'' (right item 0) or users, allowing them to assume temporary credentials. IAM policies (left item 1) are JSON documents that ''Define specific permissions'' (right item 1) for actions on AWS resources. A SageMaker execution role (left item 2) is a specific type of IAM role that ''Grants SageMaker access to resources'' (right item 2) like S3 buckets for data, or ECR for Docker images, during training and inference.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain17_3',
  NOW(),
  48,
  '{"left":["IAM roles","IAM policies","SageMaker execution role"],"right":["Delegate permissions to services","Define specific permissions","Grants SageMaker access to resources"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2],"right":[0,1,2]}'::jsonb,
  'm_17_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_17_m_17_3_121',
  'A large organization uses SageMaker Studio and needs to manage user access and isolate environments. Match the security feature to its capability.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"Multi-user isolation","B":"Access control for resources"}'::json,
  NULL,
  '''Multi-user isolation'' (left item 0) within SageMaker Studio is achieved through SageMaker Studio domains (right item 0), which provide isolated environments for different users or teams. ''Access control for resources'' (left item 1), such as S3 buckets or other AWS services accessed from Studio, is managed through IAM policies (right item 1) attached to the user''s execution role.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain17_3',
  NOW(),
  49,
  '{"left":["Multi-user isolation","Access control for resources"],"right":["SageMaker Studio domains","IAM policies"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1],"right":[0,1]}'::jsonb,
  'm_17_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_17_m_17_3_122',
  'Match Amazon VPC components to their network isolation function for SageMaker workloads.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"Security Groups","B":"Network ACLs","C":"VPC Endpoints"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'Security Groups (left item 0) act as a virtual ''Instance-level firewall'' (right item 0) for EC2 instances and other resources within a VPC, controlling inbound and outbound traffic. Network ACLs (left item 1) operate at the ''Subnet-level firewall'' (right item 1), providing an optional layer of security for traffic entering and exiting subnets. VPC Endpoints (left item 2) enable ''Private access to AWS services'' (right item 2) like S3 and SageMaker APIs from within your VPC, without requiring traffic to traverse the public internet.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain17_3',
  NOW(),
  50,
  '{"left":["Security Groups","Network ACLs","VPC Endpoints"],"right":["Instance-level firewall","Subnet-level firewall","Private access to AWS services"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2],"right":[0,1,2]}'::jsonb,
  'm_17_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_17_m_17_3_123',
  'Match a security best practice for ML solutions to its core principle.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"Least privilege","B":"Encryption by default","C":"Network segmentation"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'The principle of ''Least privilege'' (left item 0) dictates that users and services should only be granted the minimum permissions necessary to perform their tasks, which means to ''Grant minimum permissions'' (right item 0). ''Encryption by default'' (left item 1) ensures that all sensitive data, both at rest and in transit, is ''Protect[ed] data automatically'' (right item 1) without manual intervention. ''Network segmentation'' (left item 2) involves dividing networks into smaller, isolated segments to ''Isolate network traffic'' (right item 2) and limit the blast radius of security breaches.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain17_3',
  NOW(),
  51,
  '{"left":["Least privilege","Encryption by default","Network segmentation"],"right":["Grant minimum permissions","Protect data automatically","Isolate network traffic"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2],"right":[0,1,2]}'::jsonb,
  'm_17_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_17_m_17_3_124',
  'Match the AWS service to its primary auditing or logging capability for ML environments.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"AWS CloudTrail","B":"Amazon CloudWatch Logs"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'AWS CloudTrail (left item 0) is primarily used to ''Log API activity'' (right item 0) for your AWS account, recording actions taken by a user, role, or an AWS service. This is crucial for security auditing and compliance. Amazon CloudWatch Logs (left item 1) is used to ''Centralize application logs'' (right item 1) from various sources, including SageMaker training jobs and endpoints, for monitoring, storage, and analysis.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain17_3',
  NOW(),
  52,
  '{"left":["AWS CloudTrail","Amazon CloudWatch Logs"],"right":["Log API activity","Centralize application logs"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1],"right":[0,1]}'::jsonb,
  'm_17_3',
  'medium'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_17_m_17_3_125',
  'A government agency is deploying an ML model that processes classified information. All data, both when stored in Amazon S3 and when processed by Amazon SageMaker, must be encrypted with keys managed by the agency. Network traffic must also be secured to prevent eavesdropping.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"AWS KMS","B":"S3 bucket encryption","C":"SageMaker notebook encryption","D":"VPC endpoints"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'AWS KMS (Option A) is a managed service that makes it easy to create and control the encryption keys used to encrypt your data. S3 bucket encryption (Option B) ensures that objects stored in Amazon S3 are encrypted at rest. SageMaker notebook encryption (Option C) encrypts the storage volumes attached to SageMaker notebooks. VPC endpoints (Option D) provide a private connection between your VPC and supported AWS services, securing network traffic.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain17_3',
  NOW(),
  53,
  '{"left":["AWS KMS","S3 bucket encryption","SageMaker notebook encryption","VPC endpoints"],"right":["Encrypts notebook storage","Manages encryption keys","Secures network traffic","Encrypts S3 objects"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2,3],"right":[0,1,2,3]}'::jsonb,
  'm_17_3',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_17_m_17_3_126',
  'A defense contractor needs to run Amazon SageMaker training jobs and host inference endpoints in a highly isolated network environment, completely cut off from the public internet, to prevent any unauthorized data egress or ingress and meet stringent compliance.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"Amazon VPC","B":"Private Subnet","C":"Security Group","D":"VPC Endpoint"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'An Amazon VPC (Option A) provides an isolated virtual network where you can launch AWS resources. A Private Subnet (Option B) is a subnet within a VPC that does not have a route to an internet gateway, ensuring no public internet access. A Security Group (Option C) acts as a virtual firewall for instances to control inbound and outbound traffic. A VPC Endpoint (Option D) enables private connections from your VPC to supported AWS services, bypassing the public internet.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain17_3',
  NOW(),
  54,
  '{"left":["Amazon VPC","Private Subnet","Security Group","VPC Endpoint"],"right":["Controls inbound/outbound traffic","Subnet without internet gateway","Isolated virtual network","Private connection to AWS services"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2,3],"right":[0,1,2,3]}'::jsonb,
  'm_17_3',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_17_m_17_3_127',
  'An ML application integrates with several third-party APIs, requiring API keys and other credentials. The security team mandates that these secrets must be stored and retrieved securely, without being hardcoded or exposed in environment variables, to minimize risk.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"AWS Secrets Manager","B":"IAM Policy","C":"KMS Key","D":"Environment Variables"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'AWS Secrets Manager (Option A) securely stores, manages, and retrieves sensitive credentials. An IAM Policy (Option B) controls who can access secrets stored in Secrets Manager. A KMS Key (Option C) is used by Secrets Manager to encrypt the stored secrets. Using Environment Variables (Option D) is generally considered insecure for sensitive data as they can be easily accessed.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain17_3',
  NOW(),
  55,
  '{"left":["AWS Secrets Manager","IAM Policy","KMS Key","Environment Variables"],"right":["Insecure for sensitive data","Securely stores credentials","Encrypts stored secrets","Controls access to secrets"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2,3],"right":[0,1,2,3]}'::jsonb,
  'm_17_3',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_17_m_17_3_128',
  'A compliance officer requires a detailed audit trail of all actions performed on their AWS resources, especially those related to Amazon SageMaker, including who accessed what and when. They also need to understand the flow of data and models throughout the ML lifecycle.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"AWS CloudTrail","B":"Amazon CloudWatch Logs","C":"SageMaker ML Lineage Tracking","D":"IAM Access Analyzer"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'AWS CloudTrail (Option A) records API calls and events made in your AWS account, providing an audit trail. Amazon CloudWatch Logs (Option B) stores and monitors log data from various sources. Amazon SageMaker ML Lineage Tracking (Option C) tracks the steps and artifacts of an ML workflow, providing data and model lineage. IAM Access Analyzer (Option D) helps identify unintended access to your external resources.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain17_3',
  NOW(),
  56,
  '{"left":["AWS CloudTrail","Amazon CloudWatch Logs","SageMaker ML Lineage Tracking","IAM Access Analyzer"],"right":["Stores log data","Records API calls and events","Tracks ML workflow steps","Identifies unintended access"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2,3],"right":[0,1,2,3]}'::jsonb,
  'm_17_3',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_17_m_17_3_129',
  'A university research department uses Amazon SageMaker Studio for collaborative ML projects. They need to ensure that different research groups and individual students have their own isolated environments and controlled access to shared datasets, maintaining data integrity and security.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"SageMaker Studio user profiles","B":"IAM Identity Center","C":"IAM Roles","D":"Resource-based policies"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'SageMaker Studio user profiles (Option A) provide isolated environments and resources for each user within SageMaker Studio. IAM Identity Center (Option B) offers centralized identity and access management for AWS accounts and applications. IAM Roles (Option C) define permissions that can be assumed by users or services. Resource-based policies (Option D) can be attached to resources like S3 buckets to control access at a granular level.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain17_3',
  NOW(),
  57,
  '{"left":["SageMaker Studio user profiles","IAM Identity Center","IAM Roles","Resource-based policies"],"right":["Centralized identity management","Provides isolated environments","Defines permissions for users","Controls access to specific S3 buckets"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2,3],"right":[0,1,2,3]}'::jsonb,
  'm_17_3',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_17_m_17_3_130',
  'A cybersecurity team is performing a security audit of an Amazon SageMaker deployment. They are specifically looking for configurations that could lead to data exfiltration or unauthorized access from the public internet for training jobs, to ensure compliance with security policies.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"VPC-only mode","B":"Direct Internet Access","C":"Security Groups","D":"Network ACLs"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'VPC-only mode (Option A) for SageMaker training jobs ensures no public internet access, preventing data exfiltration. Direct Internet Access (Option B) allows outbound connections to the public internet, which is an anti-pattern in regulated environments. Security Groups (Option C) control inbound and outbound traffic for individual instances. Network ACLs (Option D) control traffic at the subnet level.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain17_3',
  NOW(),
  58,
  '{"left":["VPC-only mode","Direct Internet Access","Security Groups","Network ACLs"],"right":["Controls instance traffic","Allows outbound connections","Controls subnet traffic","No public internet access"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2,3],"right":[0,1,2,3]}'::jsonb,
  'm_17_3',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

INSERT INTO public.question (id, text, type, options, correct_answer, explanation, created_at, quiz_id, modified_at, index, pairs, matches, module_id, difficulty)
VALUES (
  'q_17_m_17_3_131',
  'An organization needs to implement a robust data protection and governance framework for all ML workloads running on Amazon SageMaker, covering data at rest, in transit, and ensuring clear understanding of data transformations throughout the entire ML lifecycle.',
  'matching',
  '{"A":"Encryption at rest","B":"Encryption in transit","C":"Data lineage","D":"Least privilege"}'::json,
  NULL,
  'Encryption at rest (Option A) encrypts data when it is stored, for example, in Amazon S3 or SageMaker storage volumes. Encryption in transit (Option B) encrypts data as it moves over the network between services. Data lineage (Option C), provided by SageMaker ML Lineage Tracking, tracks the transformations and dependencies of data and models. Least privilege (Option D) is a security principle that minimizes access permissions granted to users and services.',
  NOW(),
  'quiz_domain17_3',
  NOW(),
  59,
  '{"left":["Encryption at rest","Encryption in transit","Data lineage","Least privilege"],"right":["Tracks data transformations","Encrypts stored data","Minimizes access permissions","Encrypts data over network"]}'::json,
  '{"left":[0,1,2,3],"right":[0,1,2,3]}'::jsonb,
  'm_17_3',
  'hard'
) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

